{"timestamp":"2026-10-08T05:36:59.161Z","ordinal":95143,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a","turn_id":"01a1199d-3152-75c1-89b7-3e60b92f4af5","session_id":"01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a","root_turn_id":"01a1199d-3152-75c1-89b7-3e60b92f4af5","response_id":"resp_06ef5e23f2db4ce4016ac72bf2b52081918f8595c6de7c1568","usage":{"input_tokens":156498,"cached_input_tokens":152448,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":325,"reasoning_output_tokens":136,"total_tokens":156823},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2251665,"cached_input_tokens":2178176,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":8637,"reasoning_output_tokens":2079,"total_tokens":2260302},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":821022502,"cached_input_tokens":799085056,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3501214,"reasoning_output_tokens":1450284,"total_tokens":824523716}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-08T05:36:59.193Z","ordinal":95144,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a","turn_id":"01a1199d-3152-75c1-89b7-3e60b92f4af5","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-068cd11c-6e27-47be-8b57-28cb5e24e35d","process_id":"17299","command":["/bin/zsh","-c","sed -n '165,230p' docs/PARITY.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '165,230p' docs/PARITY.md","name":"PARITY.md","path":"docs/PARITY.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"The unchanged `68c883b9` complete protected SQLite/production Chrome sequence\nfails at the later saved-QR-image Attachment Capture step, before group deletion.\nAn isolated actual attachment smoke repeats the same missing-target timeout;\nthe rendered UI reports a scanner timeout and makes no successful target lookup.\nIt is not a complete-flow pass or evidence that short Unit labels caused the\nfailure. The precise QR-decoder cause, PostgreSQL snapshot/count failure,\ncomplete-flow CI, all eight full Original-UI rows and broader production\nacceptance remain open. This step is not a 100-percent or merge-ready claim.\n\n### Current independent short Unit labels (2026-10-08)\n\nThe upstream target remains `14c98284590195631750bb2352cb398ca669fe7d`,\nindependently reverified against remote `master` on 2026-10-08. Actual source\nconfiguration defaults the header to the Booklet label, navigation to the Unit\nindex and toolbar to the full Unit label. Header `UNIT_LABEL_SHORT`, navigation\n`LABEL_SHORT` and toolbar `LABEL_SHORT` now compile and render independently.\nAbsent or empty `labelshort` falls back to the selected Unit's full label.\nModern `toolbar_unit_label` takes precedence by key presence, followed by\n`toolbar_show_unit_title` and then older `unit_title`; explicit newer empty keys\ndo not fall through to older values. `HIDDEN` remains a rendering decision,\nnot an authorization or Player-metadata change.\n\nOlder immutable snapshots project their previously unsupported short-label\nsource keys when read. Explicit historical values without those source keys,\nincluding a hidden header/title, remain unchanged. This does not rewrite a\nrelease, create/reset a Run, replace a saved answer or alter navigation locks.\nThe actual facade's Verona `unitTitle` and iframe title remain the full label;\nthe visual navigation label does not remount or reconfigure the Player.\n\nFour compiler and twelve actual-facade/projection/corpus regressions run in\nthe normal test commands. All 432 core/frontend checks, typecheck and the\nproduction build pass. All 164 API tests pass separately in memory, file and\nSQLite (492 total). The official historical corpus's literal policy expectations\nadd only the new toolbar mode; its other exact assertions and vendor bytes are\nunchanged. The production initial bundle is 469.98 kB, still under the unchanged\n470-kB error budget; its existing warning thresholds are not raised.\n\nThe new `participant-current-unit-labels` section of the complete repository\nbrowser smoke uses seven checked-in, source-derived configurations and native\nBooklet 18.0 XML with aliases of the unchanged pinned Controller Unit/Player.\nIt performs real UI login in fresh contexts, independent exact labels, a\nmissing-short-label second Unit, trusted native radio input, forward/backward\nnavigation, exact durable answer and same-Run hard reload. Its owned strict\nOriginal-19/immutable-production Chrome 154 run passes all 28 combinations\n(seven configurations, both interfaces, 1280/390 widths). Operator credential\nleaks and browser page errors must be zero. Bundled Chromium 147 independently\npasses the same 28 cases on its own fixture (56 browser cases total). The newly\nextended whole sequence and fresh publication CI are separate checks.\n\nThe initial mobile Rewrite repetition fails because its nested cards shrink\nthe unchanged Player to 280 pixels while the vendor reserves `9em` on each\nside. The native radio is clipped behind the form's hit target. Original's\n390-pixel surface passes the same real input. Only mobile Rewrite Player/card\npadding is reduced; the final seven mobile Rewrite cases pass without forced\nclicks, synthetic events, added retry loops, vendor/CSS injection or sandbox changes.\n\nThe preceding unchanged `5e69fb1d` complete protected SQLite/production Chrome\nsequence also passes through monitor, exports and teardown. It is not proof\nof these new label changes. That publication still has a remote PostgreSQL UI\nfailure: group deletion reports 45 logs against a previously captured 44-log\nsnapshot. Its cause and exact deletion evidence remain to be resolved; local\nSQLite success is not PostgreSQL or merge acceptance. Toolbar on-primary\ncolors, all eight full-page Original-UI rows and broader production acceptance\nremain open. This step is not a 100-percent or merge-ready claim.\n\n### Original Controller native input after viewport rendering (2026-10-08)\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"The unchanged `68c883b9` complete protected SQLite/production Chrome sequence\nfails at the later saved-QR-image Attachment Capture step, before group deletion.\nAn isolated actual attachment smoke repeats the same missing-target timeout;\nthe rendered UI reports a scanner timeout and makes no successful target lookup.\nIt is not a complete-flow pass or evidence that short Unit labels caused the\nfailure. The precise QR-decoder cause, PostgreSQL snapshot/count failure,\ncomplete-flow CI, all eight full Original-UI rows and broader production\nacceptance remain open. This step is not a 100-percent or merge-ready claim.\n\n### Current independent short Unit labels (2026-10-08)\n\nThe upstream target remains `14c98284590195631750bb2352cb398ca669fe7d`,\nindependently reverified against remote `master` on 2026-10-08. Actual source\nconfiguration defaults the header to the Booklet label, navigation to the Unit\nindex and toolbar to the full Unit label. Header `UNIT_LABEL_SHORT`, navigation\n`LABEL_SHORT` and toolbar `LABEL_SHORT` now compile and render independently.\nAbsent or empty `labelshort` falls back to the selected Unit's full label.\nModern `toolbar_unit_label` takes precedence by key presence, followed by\n`toolbar_show_unit_title` and then older `unit_title`; explicit newer empty keys\ndo not fall through to older values. `HIDDEN` remains a rendering decision,\nnot an authorization or Player-metadata change.\n\nOlder immutable snapshots project their previously unsupported short-label\nsource keys when read. Explicit historical values without those source keys,\nincluding a hidden header/title, remain unchanged. This does not rewrite a\nrelease, create/reset a Run, replace a saved answer or alter navigation locks.\nThe actual facade's Verona `unitTitle` and iframe title remain the full label;\nthe visual navigation label does not remount or reconfigure the Player.\n\nFour compiler and twelve actual-facade/projection/corpus regressions run in\nthe normal test commands. All 432 core/frontend checks, typecheck and the\nproduction build pass. All 164 API tests pass separately in memory, file and\nSQLite (492 total). The official historical corpus's literal policy expectations\nadd only the new toolbar mode; its other exact assertions and vendor bytes are\nunchanged. The production initial bundle is 469.98 kB, still under the unchanged\n470-kB error budget; its existing warning thresholds are not raised.\n\nThe new `participant-current-unit-labels` section of the complete repository\nbrowser smoke uses seven checked-in, source-derived configurations and native\nBooklet 18.0 XML with aliases of the unchanged pinned Controller Unit/Player.\nIt performs real UI login in fresh contexts, independent exact labels, a\nmissing-short-label second Unit, trusted native radio input, forward/backward\nnavigation, exact durable answer and same-Run hard reload. Its owned strict\nOriginal-19/immutable-production Chrome 154 run passes all 28 combinations\n(seven configurations, both interfaces, 1280/390 widths). Operator credential\nleaks and browser page errors must be zero. Bundled Chromium 147 independently\npasses the same 28 cases on its own fixture (56 browser cases total). The newly\nextended whole sequence and fresh publication CI are separate checks.\n\nThe initial mobile Rewrite repetition fails because its nested cards shrink\nthe unchanged Player to 280 pixels while the vendor reserves `9em` on each\nside. The native radio is clipped behind the form's hit target. Original's\n390-pixel surface passes the same real input. Only mobile Rewrite Player/card\npadding is reduced; the final seven mobile Rewrite cases pass without forced\nclicks, synthetic events, added retry loops, vendor/CSS injection or sandbox changes.\n\nThe preceding unchanged `5e69fb1d` complete protected SQLite/production Chrome\nsequence also passes through monitor, exports and teardown. It is not proof\nof these new label changes. That publication still has a remote PostgreSQL UI\nfailure: group deletion reports 45 logs against a previously captured 44-log\nsnapshot. Its cause and exact deletion evidence remain to be resolved; local\nSQLite success is not PostgreSQL or merge acceptance. Toolbar on-primary\ncolors, all eight full-page Original-UI rows and broader production acceptance\nremain open. This step is not a 100-percent or merge-ready claim.\n\n### Original Controller native input after viewport rendering (2026-10-08)\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":10375},"formatted_output":"The unchanged `68c883b9` complete protected SQLite/production Chrome sequence\nfails at the later saved-QR-image Attachment Capture step, before group deletion.\nAn isolated actual attachment smoke repeats the same missing-target timeout;\nthe rendered UI reports a scanner timeout and makes no successful target lookup.\nIt is not a complete-flow pass or evidence that short Unit labels caused the\nfailure. The precise QR-decoder cause, PostgreSQL snapshot/count failure,\ncomplete-flow CI, all eight full Original-UI rows and broader production\nacceptance remain open. This step is not a 100-percent or merge-ready claim.\n\n### Current independent short Unit labels (2026-10-08)\n\nThe upstream target remains `14c98284590195631750bb2352cb398ca669fe7d`,\nindependently reverified against remote `master` on 2026-10-08. Actual source\nconfiguration defaults the header to the Booklet label, navigation to the Unit\nindex and toolbar to the full Unit label. Header `UNIT_LABEL_SHORT`, navigation\n`LABEL_SHORT` and toolbar `LABEL_SHORT` now compile and render independently.\nAbsent or empty `labelshort` falls back to the selected Unit's full label.\nModern `toolbar_unit_label` takes precedence by key presence, followed by\n`toolbar_show_unit_title` and then older `unit_title`; explicit newer empty keys\ndo not fall through to older values. `HIDDEN` remains a rendering decision,\nnot an authorization or Player-metadata change.\n\nOlder immutable snapshots project their previously unsupported short-label\nsource keys when read. Explicit historical values without those source keys,\nincluding a hidden header/title, remain unchanged. This does not rewrite a\nrelease, create/reset a Run, replace a saved answer or alter navigation locks.\nThe actual facade's Verona `unitTitle` and iframe title remain the full label;\nthe visual navigation label does not remount or reconfigure the Player.\n\nFour compiler and twelve actual-facade/projection/corpus regressions run in\nthe normal test commands. All 432 core/frontend checks, typecheck and the\nproduction build pass. All 164 API tests pass separately in memory, file and\nSQLite (492 total). The official historical corpus's literal policy expectations\nadd only the new toolbar mode; its other exact assertions and vendor bytes are\nunchanged. The production initial bundle is 469.98 kB, still under the unchanged\n470-kB error budget; its existing warning thresholds are not raised.\n\nThe new `participant-current-unit-labels` section of the complete repository\nbrowser smoke uses seven checked-in, source-derived configurations and native\nBooklet 18.0 XML with aliases of the unchanged pinned Controller Unit/Player.\nIt performs real UI login in fresh contexts, independent exact labels, a\nmissing-short-label second Unit, trusted native radio input, forward/backward\nnavigation, exact durable answer and same-Run hard reload. Its owned strict\nOriginal-19/immutable-production Chrome 154 run passes all 28 combinations\n(seven configurations, both interfaces, 1280/390 widths). Operator credential\nleaks and browser page errors must be zero. Bundled Chromium 147 independently\npasses the same 28 cases on its own fixture (56 browser cases total). The newly\nextended whole sequence and fresh publication CI are separate checks.\n\nThe initial mobile Rewrite repetition fails because its nested cards shrink\nthe unchanged Player to 280 pixels while the vendor reserves `9em` on each\nside. The native radio is clipped behind the form's hit target. Original's\n390-pixel surface passes the same real input. Only mobile Rewrite Player/card\npadding is reduced; the final seven mobile Rewrite cases pass without forced\nclicks, synthetic events, added retry loops, vendor/CSS injection or sandbox changes.\n\nThe preceding unchanged `5e69fb1d` complete protected SQLite/production Chrome\nsequence also passes through monitor, exports and teardown. It is not proof\nof these new label changes. That publication still has a remote PostgreSQL UI\nfailure: group deletion reports 45 logs against a previously captured 44-log\nsnapshot. Its cause and exact deletion evidence remain to be resolved; local\nSQLite success is not PostgreSQL or merge acceptance. Toolbar on-primary\ncolors, all eight full-page Original-UI rows and broader production acceptance\nremain open. This step is not a 100-percent or merge-ready claim.\n\n### Original Controller native input after viewport rendering (2026-10-08)\n"},"started_at_ms":1791437819192,"completed_at_ms":1791437819193}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-08T05:36:59.230Z","ordinal":95145,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a","turn_id":"01a1199d-3152-75c1-89b7-3e60b92f4af5","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-32457364-cda1-4cb6-b037-b4a188e4e16f","process_id":"71787","command":["/bin/zsh","-c","cat /tmp/playwright-test-short-unit-labels-20261008.js"],"cwd":"file:///Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-08-13/arbeite-im-repo-users-julian-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat /tmp/playwright-test-short-unit-labels-20261008.js","name":"playwright-test-short-unit-labels-20261008.js","path":"/tmp/playwright-test-short-unit-labels-20261008.js"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"const TARGET_FRONTEND_ROOT = process.env.TARGET_FRONTEND_ROOT;\nif (!TARGET_FRONTEND_ROOT) throw new Error('Immutable production frontend required.');\n(async () => {\n  const assert = require('node:assert/strict');\n  const { spawn } = require('node:child_process');\n  const fs = require('node:fs/promises');\n  const { join } = require('node:path');\n  const { tmpdir } = require('node:os');\n  const { pathToFileURL } = require('node:url');\n  const { brotliDecompressSync } = require('node:zlib');\n  const { chromium } = require('playwright');\n  const projectRoot = '/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app';\n  const ts = require(require.resolve('typescript', { paths: [projectRoot] }));\n  process.chdir(projectRoot);\n  const root = await fs.mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), 'testcenter-short-labels-browser-'));\n  console.log('owned_unit_label_artifacts=' + root);\n  const source = await fs.readFile(join(projectRoot, 'scripts/smoke-ui.mjs'), 'utf8');\n  const ast = ts.createSourceFile('smoke-ui.mjs', source, ts.ScriptTarget.ES2022, true, ts.ScriptKind.JS);\n  const zipNames = ['crc32Table', 'crc32', 'createStoredZipBuffer'];\n  const zipDeclarations = [];\n  const visit = node => {\n    if (ts.isVariableDeclaration(node) && zipNames.includes(node.name.getText(ast))) zipDeclarations.push(node.getText(ast));\n    ts.forEachChild(node, visit);\n  };\n  visit(ast);\n  assert.equal(zipDeclarations.length, zipNames.length);\n  const { createStoredZipBuffer } = await import('data:text/javascript;base64,' + Buffer.from(\n    zipDeclarations.map(text => 'const ' + text + ';').join('\\n') + '\\nexport { createStoredZipBuffer };').toString('base64'));\n  const corpusRoot = join(projectRoot, 'test-fixtures/original-testcenter');\n  const corpus = JSON.parse(await fs.readFile(join(corpusRoot, 'corpus.json'), 'utf8'));\n  const official = corpus.currentOriginalTestControllerPackage;\n  const unitFixture = official.units.find(item => item[1] === 'CY-Unit.Sample-101');\n  const unit = Buffer.from((await fs.readFile(join(corpusRoot, unitFixture[0]), 'utf8')).trim(), 'base64').toString('utf8');\n  const player = brotliDecompressSync(Buffer.from(await fs.readFile(join(corpusRoot, official.player.fixture), 'utf8'), 'base64')).toString('utf8');\n  const { cases } = JSON.parse(await fs.readFile(join(corpusRoot, 'current-unit-label-cases.json'), 'utf8'));\n  const xmlEscape = value => value.replaceAll('&', '&amp;').replaceAll('\"', '&quot;').replaceAll('<', '&lt;');\n  const fullA = 'Volle Aufgabe ä/β';\n  const fullB = 'Zweite volle Aufgabe ä/β';\n  const shortA = 'Kurz ä/β';\n  const booklets = cases.map(item => ({ fileName: 'booklets/' + item.key + '.xml', content:\n    '<?xml version=\"1.0\"?><Booklet xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation=\"https://w3id.org/iqb/spec/testcenter-booklet-xml/18.0\">' +\n    '<Metadata><Id>labels-' + item.key + '</Id><Label>Label booklet ' + item.key + '</Label></Metadata><BookletConfig>' +\n    Object.entries({ pagingMode: 'buttons', navbar_forward_button: 'UNITS', navbar_backward_button: 'UNITS', unit_responses_buffer_time: '0', ...item.config })\n      .map(([key, value]) => '<Config key=\"' + key + '\">' + xmlEscape(value) + '</Config>').join('') +\n    '</BookletConfig><Units><Testlet id=\"owned-block\" label=\"Owned block\"><Unit id=\"CY-Unit.Sample-101\" alias=\"a\" label=\"' + fullA + '\" labelshort=\"' + shortA + '\"/>' +\n    '<Unit id=\"CY-Unit.Sample-101\" alias=\"b\" label=\"' + fullB + '\"/></Testlet></Units></Booklet>' }));\n  const archive = createStoredZipBuffer([...booklets, { fileName: 'units/CY_Unit101.xml', content: unit },\n    { fileName: 'players/verona-player-simple-6.0.html', content: player }]);\n  const apiModule = pathToFileURL(join(projectRoot, 'apps/api/dist/apps/api/src/index.js')).href;\n  const server = spawn(process.execPath, ['--input-type=module', '-e', `\n    import { createProductionApiServer } from ${JSON.stringify(apiModule)};\n    const server = await createProductionApiServer();\n    server.listen(0, '127.0.0.1', () => process.send({ port: server.address().port }));\n    process.once('SIGTERM', () => server.close(() => process.exit(0)));\n  `], { cwd: TARGET_FRONTEND_ROOT, stdio: ['ignore', 'ignore', 'inherit', 'ipc'], env: { ...process.env,\n    FIRST_SLICE_STORE: 'sqlite', FIRST_SLICE_SQLITE_FILE: join(root, 'owned.sqlite'),\n    FIRST_SLICE_BOOTSTRAP_DEMO: 'true', FIRST_SLICE_OPERATOR_AUTH_REQUIRED: 'true',\n    FIRST_SLICE_XML_SCHEMA_PROFILE: 'original-19', FIRST_SLICE_XML_SCHEMA_DOWNLOAD: 'false',\n    FIRST_SLICE_XML_SCHEMA_CACHE: join(projectRoot, '.data/original-xml-schemas') } });\n  let browser;\n  let page;\n  let context;\n  try {\n    const port = await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n      const timer = setTimeout(() => reject(new Error('Owned API startup timed out')), 20000);\n      server.once('message', value => { clearTimeout(timer); resolve(value.port); });\n      server.once('error', error => { clearTimeout(timer); reject(error); });\n      server.once('exit', () => { clearTimeout(timer); reject(new Error('Owned API exited before ready')); });\n    });\n    const baseUrl = 'http://127.0.0.1:' + port;\n    console.log('owned_unit_label_base_url=' + baseUrl);\n    let operatorToken;\n    const api = async (path, body, token = operatorToken) => {\n      const response = await fetch(baseUrl + path, { method: body === undefined ? 'GET' : 'POST',\n        headers: { ...(body === undefined ? {} : { 'content-type': 'application/json' }), ...(token ? { authorization: 'Bearer ' + token } : {}) },\n        ...(body === undefined ? {} : { body: JSON.stringify(body) }) });\n      const value = await response.json();\n      assert.ok(response.ok, path + ': ' + response.status + ' ' + JSON.stringify(value));\n      return value;\n    };\n    operatorToken = (await api('/api/v1/admin/auth/sign-in', { username: 'demo-admin', password: 'REDACTED' })).sessionToken;\n    if (process.env.LABEL_REPOSITORY_GATE) {\n      browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: false, channel: process.env.LABEL_BROWSER_CHANNEL || 'chrome' });\n      console.log('unit_label_browser=' + browser.version());\n      const { runParticipantUnitLabelSmoke } = await import(pathToFileURL(join(projectRoot, 'scripts/participant-unit-label-smoke.mjs')).href);\n      await runParticipantUnitLabelSmoke({ browser, baseUrl, tenantKey: 'owned-label-tenant', workspaceKey: 'owned-labels',\n        unitDocument: unit, playerDocument: player, createZip: createStoredZipBuffer, operatorToken,\n        sendJson: async (url, { body } = {}) => {\n          const response = await fetch(url, { method: 'POST', headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json', authorization: 'Bearer ' + operatorToken }, body: JSON.stringify(body) });\n          assert.ok(response.ok, url + ': ' + response.status);\n          return response;\n        } });\n      return;\n    }\n    await api('/api/v1/tenants/demo-tenant/workspaces', { workspaceKey: 'owned-labels', displayName: 'Owned short Unit label acceptance' });\n    const workspace = '/api/v1/tenants/demo-tenant/workspaces/owned-labels';\n    const uploaded = await api(workspace + '/source-packages', { fileName: 'owned-labels.zip', mediaType: 'application/zip', sourceDocument: 'data:application/zip;base64,' + archive.toString('base64') });\n    const imported = await api(workspace + '/import-jobs', { sourcePackageId: uploaded.sourcePackage.sourcePackageId });\n    assert.equal(imported.importJob.status, 'completed', JSON.stringify(imported.importJob.diagnostics));\n    assert.ok(imported.stagedContentRelease?.contentReleaseId);\n    await api(workspace + '/content-releases/' + imported.stagedContentRelease.contentReleaseId + '/activate', {});\n    await api(workspace + '/participant-roster', { rosterText: ['rewrite', 'original'].flatMap(ui => [1280, 390].flatMap(width => cases.map(item => ({\n      loginKey: 'labels-' + item.key + '-' + ui + '-' + width, groupKey: 'owned-labels', bookletKey: 'labels-' + item.key, mode: 'run-hot-return'\n    })))) });\n    browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: false, channel: process.env.LABEL_BROWSER_CHANNEL || 'chrome' });\n    console.log('unit_label_browser=' + browser.version());\n    const interfaces = process.env.LABEL_INTERFACES?.split(',') || ['rewrite', 'original'];\n    const widths = process.env.LABEL_WIDTHS?.split(',').map(Number) || [1280, 390];\n    for (const ui of interfaces) for (const width of widths) for (const item of cases.filter(item => !process.env.LABEL_CASE || item.key === process.env.LABEL_CASE)) {\n      const loginKey = 'labels-' + item.key + '-' + ui + '-' + width;\n      context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width, height: 900 } });\n      await context.tracing.start({ screenshots: true, snapshots: true, sources: true });\n      page = await context.newPage();\n      const errors = [];\n      page.on('pageerror', error => errors.push(String(error)));\n      let operatorLeaks = 0;\n      page.on('request', request => {\n        if (request.url().includes('/api/v1/participant/') && request.headers().authorization === 'Bearer ' + operatorToken) operatorLeaks++;\n      });\n      await page.goto(baseUrl + '/app/participant?' + new URLSearchParams({ ui, tenantKey: 'demo-tenant', workspaceKey: 'owned-labels' }), { waitUntil: 'networkidle' });\n      if (ui === 'original') await page.getByLabel('Anmeldename', { exact: true }).fill(loginKey);\n      else await page.locator('#participantLoginKey').fill(loginKey);\n      const signingIn = page.waitForResponse(response => new URL(response.url()).pathname === '/api/v1/participant/auth/sign-in');\n      const resuming = page.waitForResponse(response => /\\/sessions\\/[^/]+\\/resume$/.test(new URL(response.url()).pathname));\n      if (ui === 'original') await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Weiter', exact: true }).click();\n      else await page.locator('#participantRouteSignInButton').click();\n      const signedIn = await signingIn;\n      assert.equal(signedIn.status(), 200);\n      const identity = await signedIn.json();\n      assert.notEqual(identity.sessionToken, operatorToken);\n      // A single assigned saving Booklet starts through the real automatic\n      // participant-entry workflow. Observe its request before submitting login.\n      const resumed = await resuming;\n      assert.equal(resumed.status(), 200);\n      const runId = (await resumed.json()).testRun.testRunId;\n      const state = () => api('/api/v1/participant/sessions/' + identity.participantSession.participantSessionId + '/current-state?testRunId=' + runId, undefined, identity.sessionToken);\n      await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerVersion').filter({ hasText: 'API 6.0' }).waitFor({ state: ui === 'original' ? 'attached' : 'visible' });\n      const assertLabels = async (full, short, position) => {\n        const waitText = (selector, expected) => page.waitForFunction(({ selector, expected }) =>\n          document.querySelector(selector)?.textContent?.trim().replace(/\\s+/g, ' ') === expected, { selector, expected });\n        await page.waitForFunction(expected => document.querySelector('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame')?.getAttribute('title') === expected, full);\n        const chosen = mode => mode === 'short' ? short || full : mode === 'booklet' ? 'Label booklet ' + item.key : full;\n        const headerSelector = ui === 'original' ? '#participantApplicationHeader h1' : '#participantRouteScreenHeader';\n        const header = page.locator(headerSelector);\n        await waitText(headerSelector, chosen(item.header));\n        assert.equal((await header.textContent()).trim(), chosen(item.header));\n        const toolbarSelector = ui === 'original' ? '#originalPlayerToolbar [data-cy=\"unit-title\"]' : '#participantRouteUnit';\n        const toolbar = page.locator(toolbarSelector);\n        if (item.toolbar === 'hidden') assert.equal(await toolbar.count(), 0);\n        else { await waitText(toolbarSelector, chosen(item.toolbar)); assert.equal((await toolbar.textContent()).trim(), chosen(item.toolbar)); }\n        const navigation = page.locator(ui === 'original' ? '#originalUnitNavigation-label' : '#participantRouteUnitNavigationLabel');\n        if (item.nav === 'hidden') assert.equal(await navigation.count(), 0);\n        else {\n          const expected = item.nav === 'index' ? (ui === 'original' ? 'Aufgabe ' + position + '/2' : 'Unit ' + position + ' / 2') : chosen(item.nav);\n          await waitText(ui === 'original' ? '#originalUnitNavigation-label' : '#participantRouteUnitNavigationLabel', expected);\n          assert.equal((await navigation.textContent()).trim().replace(/\\s+/g, ' '), expected);\n        }\n        assert.equal(await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').getAttribute('title'), full);\n      };\n      await assertLabels(fullA, shortA, 1);\n      const firstState = await state();\n      assert.equal(firstState.currentRunState.bookletUnits[0].shortLabel, shortA);\n      assert.equal(firstState.currentRunState.bookletUnits[1].shortLabel, undefined);\n      await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').scrollIntoViewIfNeeded();\n      await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').screenshot();\n      const radio = page.frameLocator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').locator('[data-cy=\"TestController-radio1-Aufg1\"]');\n      if (process.env.LABEL_DIAGNOSTICS) {\n        console.log('unit_label_geometry=' + JSON.stringify({ ui, width, key: item.key,\n          owner: await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').boundingBox(),\n          radio: await radio.boundingBox(),\n          inner: await radio.evaluate(element => ({ width: innerWidth, height: innerHeight, scrollX, scrollY,\n            box: element.getBoundingClientRect().toJSON(), checked: element.checked,\n            hit: document.elementFromPoint(element.getBoundingClientRect().x + element.getBoundingClientRect().width / 2,\n              element.getBoundingClientRect().y + element.getBoundingClientRect().height / 2)?.outerHTML.slice(0, 300) })) }));\n      }\n      await radio.check();\n      let saved;\n      for (let attempt = 0; attempt < 100; attempt++) {\n        const snapshot = await state();\n        const raw = snapshot.currentRunState.testRun.unitResponses.a;\n        if (raw && JSON.parse(raw).unitState?.dataParts?.answers?.includes('VALUE_CHANGED')) { saved = raw; break; }\n        await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 100));\n      }\n      assert.ok(saved, 'Native radio answer must be durably saved');\n      await page.locator(ui === 'original' ? '#participantVeronaGlobalForwardButton' : '#participantRouteNextUnitButton').click();\n      await assertLabels(fullB, undefined, 2);\n      await page.locator(ui === 'original' ? '#participantVeronaGlobalBackwardButton' : '#participantRoutePreviousUnitButton').click();\n      await assertLabels(fullA, shortA, 1);\n      assert.equal((await state()).currentRunState.testRun.unitResponses.a, saved);\n      await page.reload({ waitUntil: 'networkidle' });\n      await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerVersion').filter({ hasText: 'API 6.0' }).waitFor({ state: ui === 'original' ? 'attached' : 'visible' });\n      await assertLabels(fullA, shortA, 1);\n      assert.equal((await state()).currentRunState.testRun.testRunId, runId);\n      assert.equal((await state()).currentRunState.testRun.unitResponses.a, saved);\n      assert.equal(await page.frameLocator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').locator('[data-cy=\"TestController-radio1-Aufg1\"]').isChecked(), true);\n      assert.equal(operatorLeaks, 0);\n      assert.deepEqual(errors, []);\n      await page.screenshot({ path: join(root, ui + '-' + width + '-' + item.key + '.png'), fullPage: true });\n      await context.tracing.stop({ path: join(root, ui + '-' + width + '-' + item.key + '.zip') });\n      await context.close();\n      context = null;\n      console.log('unit_labels=' + ui + '/' + width + '/' + item.key + ':passed');\n    }\n    console.log('unit_labels_all_selected_cases_passed=true');\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (page) await page.screenshot({ path: join(root, 'failure.png'), fullPage: true }).catch(() => {});\n    if (context) await context.tracing.stop({ path: join(root, 'failure.zip') }).catch(() => {});\n    throw error;\n  } finally {\n    await browser?.close();\n    const exited = new Promise(resolve => server.once('exit', resolve));\n    server.kill('SIGTERM');\n    await Promise.race([exited, new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 5000))]);\n    if (server.exitCode === null) server.kill('SIGKILL');\n  }\n})().catch(error => { console.error('unit_label_browser_error=' + error.message); process.exitCode = 1; });\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"const TARGET_FRONTEND_ROOT = process.env.TARGET_FRONTEND_ROOT;\nif (!TARGET_FRONTEND_ROOT) throw new Error('Immutable production frontend required.');\n(async () => {\n  const assert = require('node:assert/strict');\n  const { spawn } = require('node:child_process');\n  const fs = require('node:fs/promises');\n  const { join } = require('node:path');\n  const { tmpdir } = require('node:os');\n  const { pathToFileURL } = require('node:url');\n  const { brotliDecompressSync } = require('node:zlib');\n  const { chromium } = require('playwright');\n  const projectRoot = '/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app';\n  const ts = require(require.resolve('typescript', { paths: [projectRoot] }));\n  process.chdir(projectRoot);\n  const root = await fs.mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), 'testcenter-short-labels-browser-'));\n  console.log('owned_unit_label_artifacts=' + root);\n  const source = await fs.readFile(join(projectRoot, 'scripts/smoke-ui.mjs'), 'utf8');\n  const ast = ts.createSourceFile('smoke-ui.mjs', source, ts.ScriptTarget.ES2022, true, ts.ScriptKind.JS);\n  const zipNames = ['crc32Table', 'crc32', 'createStoredZipBuffer'];\n  const zipDeclarations = [];\n  const visit = node => {\n    if (ts.isVariableDeclaration(node) && zipNames.includes(node.name.getText(ast))) zipDeclarations.push(node.getText(ast));\n    ts.forEachChild(node, visit);\n  };\n  visit(ast);\n  assert.equal(zipDeclarations.length, zipNames.length);\n  const { createStoredZipBuffer } = await import('data:text/javascript;base64,' + Buffer.from(\n    zipDeclarations.map(text => 'const ' + text + ';').join('\\n') + '\\nexport { createStoredZipBuffer };').toString('base64'));\n  const corpusRoot = join(projectRoot, 'test-fixtures/original-testcenter');\n  const corpus = JSON.parse(await fs.readFile(join(corpusRoot, 'corpus.json'), 'utf8'));\n  const official = corpus.currentOriginalTestControllerPackage;\n  const unitFixture = official.units.find(item => item[1] === 'CY-Unit.Sample-101');\n  const unit = Buffer.from((await fs.readFile(join(corpusRoot, unitFixture[0]), 'utf8')).trim(), 'base64').toString('utf8');\n  const player = brotliDecompressSync(Buffer.from(await fs.readFile(join(corpusRoot, official.player.fixture), 'utf8'), 'base64')).toString('utf8');\n  const { cases } = JSON.parse(await fs.readFile(join(corpusRoot, 'current-unit-label-cases.json'), 'utf8'));\n  const xmlEscape = value => value.replaceAll('&', '&amp;').replaceAll('\"', '&quot;').replaceAll('<', '&lt;');\n  const fullA = 'Volle Aufgabe ä/β';\n  const fullB = 'Zweite volle Aufgabe ä/β';\n  const shortA = 'Kurz ä/β';\n  const booklets = cases.map(item => ({ fileName: 'booklets/' + item.key + '.xml', content:\n    '<?xml version=\"1.0\"?><Booklet xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation=\"https://w3id.org/iqb/spec/testcenter-booklet-xml/18.0\">' +\n    '<Metadata><Id>labels-' + item.key + '</Id><Label>Label booklet ' + item.key + '</Label></Metadata><BookletConfig>' +\n    Object.entries({ pagingMode: 'buttons', navbar_forward_button: 'UNITS', navbar_backward_button: 'UNITS', unit_responses_buffer_time: '0', ...item.config })\n      .map(([key, value]) => '<Config key=\"' + key + '\">' + xmlEscape(value) + '</Config>').join('') +\n    '</BookletConfig><Units><Testlet id=\"owned-block\" label=\"Owned block\"><Unit id=\"CY-Unit.Sample-101\" alias=\"a\" label=\"' + fullA + '\" labelshort=\"' + shortA + '\"/>' +\n    '<Unit id=\"CY-Unit.Sample-101\" alias=\"b\" label=\"' + fullB + '\"/></Testlet></Units></Booklet>' }));\n  const archive = createStoredZipBuffer([...booklets, { fileName: 'units/CY_Unit101.xml', content: unit },\n    { fileName: 'players/verona-player-simple-6.0.html', content: player }]);\n  const apiModule = pathToFileURL(join(projectRoot, 'apps/api/dist/apps/api/src/index.js')).href;\n  const server = spawn(process.execPath, ['--input-type=module', '-e', `\n    import { createProductionApiServer } from ${JSON.stringify(apiModule)};\n    const server = await createProductionApiServer();\n    server.listen(0, '127.0.0.1', () => process.send({ port: server.address().port }));\n    process.once('SIGTERM', () => server.close(() => process.exit(0)));\n  `], { cwd: TARGET_FRONTEND_ROOT, stdio: ['ignore', 'ignore', 'inherit', 'ipc'], env: { ...process.env,\n    FIRST_SLICE_STORE: 'sqlite', FIRST_SLICE_SQLITE_FILE: join(root, 'owned.sqlite'),\n    FIRST_SLICE_BOOTSTRAP_DEMO: 'true', FIRST_SLICE_OPERATOR_AUTH_REQUIRED: 'true',\n    FIRST_SLICE_XML_SCHEMA_PROFILE: 'original-19', FIRST_SLICE_XML_SCHEMA_DOWNLOAD: 'false',\n    FIRST_SLICE_XML_SCHEMA_CACHE: join(projectRoot, '.data/original-xml-schemas') } });\n  let browser;\n  let page;\n  let context;\n  try {\n    const port = await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n      const timer = setTimeout(() => reject(new Error('Owned API startup timed out')), 20000);\n      server.once('message', value => { clearTimeout(timer); resolve(value.port); });\n      server.once('error', error => { clearTimeout(timer); reject(error); });\n      server.once('exit', () => { clearTimeout(timer); reject(new Error('Owned API exited before ready')); });\n    });\n    const baseUrl = 'http://127.0.0.1:' + port;\n    console.log('owned_unit_label_base_url=' + baseUrl);\n    let operatorToken;\n    const api = async (path, body, token = operatorToken) => {\n      const response = await fetch(baseUrl + path, { method: body === undefined ? 'GET' : 'POST',\n        headers: { ...(body === undefined ? {} : { 'content-type': 'application/json' }), ...(token ? { authorization: 'Bearer ' + token } : {}) },\n        ...(body === undefined ? {} : { body: JSON.stringify(body) }) });\n      const value = await response.json();\n      assert.ok(response.ok, path + ': ' + response.status + ' ' + JSON.stringify(value));\n      return value;\n    };\n    operatorToken = (await api('/api/v1/admin/auth/sign-in', { username: 'demo-admin', password: 'REDACTED' })).sessionToken;\n    if (process.env.LABEL_REPOSITORY_GATE) {\n      browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: false, channel: process.env.LABEL_BROWSER_CHANNEL || 'chrome' });\n      console.log('unit_label_browser=' + browser.version());\n      const { runParticipantUnitLabelSmoke } = await import(pathToFileURL(join(projectRoot, 'scripts/participant-unit-label-smoke.mjs')).href);\n      await runParticipantUnitLabelSmoke({ browser, baseUrl, tenantKey: 'owned-label-tenant', workspaceKey: 'owned-labels',\n        unitDocument: unit, playerDocument: player, createZip: createStoredZipBuffer, operatorToken,\n        sendJson: async (url, { body } = {}) => {\n          const response = await fetch(url, { method: 'POST', headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json', authorization: 'Bearer ' + operatorToken }, body: JSON.stringify(body) });\n          assert.ok(response.ok, url + ': ' + response.status);\n          return response;\n        } });\n      return;\n    }\n    await api('/api/v1/tenants/demo-tenant/workspaces', { workspaceKey: 'owned-labels', displayName: 'Owned short Unit label acceptance' });\n    const workspace = '/api/v1/tenants/demo-tenant/workspaces/owned-labels';\n    const uploaded = await api(workspace + '/source-packages', { fileName: 'owned-labels.zip', mediaType: 'application/zip', sourceDocument: 'data:application/zip;base64,' + archive.toString('base64') });\n    const imported = await api(workspace + '/import-jobs', { sourcePackageId: uploaded.sourcePackage.sourcePackageId });\n    assert.equal(imported.importJob.status, 'completed', JSON.stringify(imported.importJob.diagnostics));\n    assert.ok(imported.stagedContentRelease?.contentReleaseId);\n    await api(workspace + '/content-releases/' + imported.stagedContentRelease.contentReleaseId + '/activate', {});\n    await api(workspace + '/participant-roster', { rosterText: ['rewrite', 'original'].flatMap(ui => [1280, 390].flatMap(width => cases.map(item => ({\n      loginKey: 'labels-' + item.key + '-' + ui + '-' + width, groupKey: 'owned-labels', bookletKey: 'labels-' + item.key, mode: 'run-hot-return'\n    })))) });\n    browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: false, channel: process.env.LABEL_BROWSER_CHANNEL || 'chrome' });\n    console.log('unit_label_browser=' + browser.version());\n    const interfaces = process.env.LABEL_INTERFACES?.split(',') || ['rewrite', 'original'];\n    const widths = process.env.LABEL_WIDTHS?.split(',').map(Number) || [1280, 390];\n    for (const ui of interfaces) for (const width of widths) for (const item of cases.filter(item => !process.env.LABEL_CASE || item.key === process.env.LABEL_CASE)) {\n      const loginKey = 'labels-' + item.key + '-' + ui + '-' + width;\n      context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width, height: 900 } });\n      await context.tracing.start({ screenshots: true, snapshots: true, sources: true });\n      page = await context.newPage();\n      const errors = [];\n      page.on('pageerror', error => errors.push(String(error)));\n      let operatorLeaks = 0;\n      page.on('request', request => {\n        if (request.url().includes('/api/v1/participant/') && request.headers().authorization === 'Bearer ' + operatorToken) operatorLeaks++;\n      });\n      await page.goto(baseUrl + '/app/participant?' + new URLSearchParams({ ui, tenantKey: 'demo-tenant', workspaceKey: 'owned-labels' }), { waitUntil: 'networkidle' });\n      if (ui === 'original') await page.getByLabel('Anmeldename', { exact: true }).fill(loginKey);\n      else await page.locator('#participantLoginKey').fill(loginKey);\n      const signingIn = page.waitForResponse(response => new URL(response.url()).pathname === '/api/v1/participant/auth/sign-in');\n      const resuming = page.waitForResponse(response => /\\/sessions\\/[^/]+\\/resume$/.test(new URL(response.url()).pathname));\n      if (ui === 'original') await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Weiter', exact: true }).click();\n      else await page.locator('#participantRouteSignInButton').click();\n      const signedIn = await signingIn;\n      assert.equal(signedIn.status(), 200);\n      const identity = await signedIn.json();\n      assert.notEqual(identity.sessionToken, operatorToken);\n      // A single assigned saving Booklet starts through the real automatic\n      // participant-entry workflow. Observe its request before submitting login.\n      const resumed = await resuming;\n      assert.equal(resumed.status(), 200);\n      const runId = (await resumed.json()).testRun.testRunId;\n      const state = () => api('/api/v1/participant/sessions/' + identity.participantSession.participantSessionId + '/current-state?testRunId=' + runId, undefined, identity.sessionToken);\n      await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerVersion').filter({ hasText: 'API 6.0' }).waitFor({ state: ui === 'original' ? 'attached' : 'visible' });\n      const assertLabels = async (full, short, position) => {\n        const waitText = (selector, expected) => page.waitForFunction(({ selector, expected }) =>\n          document.querySelector(selector)?.textContent?.trim().replace(/\\s+/g, ' ') === expected, { selector, expected });\n        await page.waitForFunction(expected => document.querySelector('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame')?.getAttribute('title') === expected, full);\n        const chosen = mode => mode === 'short' ? short || full : mode === 'booklet' ? 'Label booklet ' + item.key : full;\n        const headerSelector = ui === 'original' ? '#participantApplicationHeader h1' : '#participantRouteScreenHeader';\n        const header = page.locator(headerSelector);\n        await waitText(headerSelector, chosen(item.header));\n        assert.equal((await header.textContent()).trim(), chosen(item.header));\n        const toolbarSelector = ui === 'original' ? '#originalPlayerToolbar [data-cy=\"unit-title\"]' : '#participantRouteUnit';\n        const toolbar = page.locator(toolbarSelector);\n        if (item.toolbar === 'hidden') assert.equal(await toolbar.count(), 0);\n        else { await waitText(toolbarSelector, chosen(item.toolbar)); assert.equal((await toolbar.textContent()).trim(), chosen(item.toolbar)); }\n        const navigation = page.locator(ui === 'original' ? '#originalUnitNavigation-label' : '#participantRouteUnitNavigationLabel');\n        if (item.nav === 'hidden') assert.equal(await navigation.count(), 0);\n        else {\n          const expected = item.nav === 'index' ? (ui === 'original' ? 'Aufgabe ' + position + '/2' : 'Unit ' + position + ' / 2') : chosen(item.nav);\n          await waitText(ui === 'original' ? '#originalUnitNavigation-label' : '#participantRouteUnitNavigationLabel', expected);\n          assert.equal((await navigation.textContent()).trim().replace(/\\s+/g, ' '), expected);\n        }\n        assert.equal(await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').getAttribute('title'), full);\n      };\n      await assertLabels(fullA, shortA, 1);\n      const firstState = await state();\n      assert.equal(firstState.currentRunState.bookletUnits[0].shortLabel, shortA);\n      assert.equal(firstState.currentRunState.bookletUnits[1].shortLabel, undefined);\n      await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').scrollIntoViewIfNeeded();\n      await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').screenshot();\n      const radio = page.frameLocator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').locator('[data-cy=\"TestController-radio1-Aufg1\"]');\n      if (process.env.LABEL_DIAGNOSTICS) {\n        console.log('unit_label_geometry=' + JSON.stringify({ ui, width, key: item.key,\n          owner: await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').boundingBox(),\n          radio: await radio.boundingBox(),\n          inner: await radio.evaluate(element => ({ width: innerWidth, height: innerHeight, scrollX, scrollY,\n            box: element.getBoundingClientRect().toJSON(), checked: element.checked,\n            hit: document.elementFromPoint(element.getBoundingClientRect().x + element.getBoundingClientRect().width / 2,\n              element.getBoundingClientRect().y + element.getBoundingClientRect().height / 2)?.outerHTML.slice(0, 300) })) }));\n      }\n      await radio.check();\n      let saved;\n      for (let attempt = 0; attempt < 100; attempt++) {\n        const snapshot = await state();\n        const raw = snapshot.currentRunState.testRun.unitResponses.a;\n        if (raw && JSON.parse(raw).unitState?.dataParts?.answers?.includes('VALUE_CHANGED')) { saved = raw; break; }\n        await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 100));\n      }\n      assert.ok(saved, 'Native radio answer must be durably saved');\n      await page.locator(ui === 'original' ? '#participantVeronaGlobalForwardButton' : '#participantRouteNextUnitButton').click();\n      await assertLabels(fullB, undefined, 2);\n      await page.locator(ui === 'original' ? '#participantVeronaGlobalBackwardButton' : '#participantRoutePreviousUnitButton').click();\n      await assertLabels(fullA, shortA, 1);\n      assert.equal((await state()).currentRunState.testRun.unitResponses.a, saved);\n      await page.reload({ waitUntil: 'networkidle' });\n      await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerVersion').filter({ hasText: 'API 6.0' }).waitFor({ state: ui === 'original' ? 'attached' : 'visible' });\n      await assertLabels(fullA, shortA, 1);\n      assert.equal((await state()).currentRunState.testRun.testRunId, runId);\n      assert.equal((await state()).currentRunState.testRun.unitResponses.a, saved);\n      assert.equal(await page.frameLocator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').locator('[data-cy=\"TestController-radio1-Aufg1\"]').isChecked(), true);\n      assert.equal(operatorLeaks, 0);\n      assert.deepEqual(errors, []);\n      await page.screenshot({ path: join(root, ui + '-' + width + '-' + item.key + '.png'), fullPage: true });\n      await context.tracing.stop({ path: join(root, ui + '-' + width + '-' + item.key + '.zip') });\n      await context.close();\n      context = null;\n      console.log('unit_labels=' + ui + '/' + width + '/' + item.key + ':passed');\n    }\n    console.log('unit_labels_all_selected_cases_passed=true');\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (page) await page.screenshot({ path: join(root, 'failure.png'), fullPage: true }).catch(() => {});\n    if (context) await context.tracing.stop({ path: join(root, 'failure.zip') }).catch(() => {});\n    throw error;\n  } finally {\n    await browser?.close();\n    const exited = new Promise(resolve => server.once('exit', resolve));\n    server.kill('SIGTERM');\n    await Promise.race([exited, new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 5000))]);\n    if (server.exitCode === null) server.kill('SIGKILL');\n  }\n})().catch(error => { console.error('unit_label_browser_error=' + error.message); process.exitCode = 1; });\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":7667},"formatted_output":"const TARGET_FRONTEND_ROOT = process.env.TARGET_FRONTEND_ROOT;\nif (!TARGET_FRONTEND_ROOT) throw new Error('Immutable production frontend required.');\n(async () => {\n  const assert = require('node:assert/strict');\n  const { spawn } = require('node:child_process');\n  const fs = require('node:fs/promises');\n  const { join } = require('node:path');\n  const { tmpdir } = require('node:os');\n  const { pathToFileURL } = require('node:url');\n  const { brotliDecompressSync } = require('node:zlib');\n  const { chromium } = require('playwright');\n  const projectRoot = '/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app';\n  const ts = require(require.resolve('typescript', { paths: [projectRoot] }));\n  process.chdir(projectRoot);\n  const root = await fs.mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), 'testcenter-short-labels-browser-'));\n  console.log('owned_unit_label_artifacts=' + root);\n  const source = await fs.readFile(join(projectRoot, 'scripts/smoke-ui.mjs'), 'utf8');\n  const ast = ts.createSourceFile('smoke-ui.mjs', source, ts.ScriptTarget.ES2022, true, ts.ScriptKind.JS);\n  const zipNames = ['crc32Table', 'crc32', 'createStoredZipBuffer'];\n  const zipDeclarations = [];\n  const visit = node => {\n    if (ts.isVariableDeclaration(node) && zipNames.includes(node.name.getText(ast))) zipDeclarations.push(node.getText(ast));\n    ts.forEachChild(node, visit);\n  };\n  visit(ast);\n  assert.equal(zipDeclarations.length, zipNames.length);\n  const { createStoredZipBuffer } = await import('data:text/javascript;base64,' + Buffer.from(\n    zipDeclarations.map(text => 'const ' + text + ';').join('\\n') + '\\nexport { createStoredZipBuffer };').toString('base64'));\n  const corpusRoot = join(projectRoot, 'test-fixtures/original-testcenter');\n  const corpus = JSON.parse(await fs.readFile(join(corpusRoot, 'corpus.json'), 'utf8'));\n  const official = corpus.currentOriginalTestControllerPackage;\n  const unitFixture = official.units.find(item => item[1] === 'CY-Unit.Sample-101');\n  const unit = Buffer.from((await fs.readFile(join(corpusRoot, unitFixture[0]), 'utf8')).trim(), 'base64').toString('utf8');\n  const player = brotliDecompressSync(Buffer.from(await fs.readFile(join(corpusRoot, official.player.fixture), 'utf8'), 'base64')).toString('utf8');\n  const { cases } = JSON.parse(await fs.readFile(join(corpusRoot, 'current-unit-label-cases.json'), 'utf8'));\n  const xmlEscape = value => value.replaceAll('&', '&amp;').replaceAll('\"', '&quot;').replaceAll('<', '&lt;');\n  const fullA = 'Volle Aufgabe ä/β';\n  const fullB = 'Zweite volle Aufgabe ä/β';\n  const shortA = 'Kurz ä/β';\n  const booklets = cases.map(item => ({ fileName: 'booklets/' + item.key + '.xml', content:\n    '<?xml version=\"1.0\"?><Booklet xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation=\"https://w3id.org/iqb/spec/testcenter-booklet-xml/18.0\">' +\n    '<Metadata><Id>labels-' + item.key + '</Id><Label>Label booklet ' + item.key + '</Label></Metadata><BookletConfig>' +\n    Object.entries({ pagingMode: 'buttons', navbar_forward_button: 'UNITS', navbar_backward_button: 'UNITS', unit_responses_buffer_time: '0', ...item.config })\n      .map(([key, value]) => '<Config key=\"' + key + '\">' + xmlEscape(value) + '</Config>').join('') +\n    '</BookletConfig><Units><Testlet id=\"owned-block\" label=\"Owned block\"><Unit id=\"CY-Unit.Sample-101\" alias=\"a\" label=\"' + fullA + '\" labelshort=\"' + shortA + '\"/>' +\n    '<Unit id=\"CY-Unit.Sample-101\" alias=\"b\" label=\"' + fullB + '\"/></Testlet></Units></Booklet>' }));\n  const archive = createStoredZipBuffer([...booklets, { fileName: 'units/CY_Unit101.xml', content: unit },\n    { fileName: 'players/verona-player-simple-6.0.html', content: player }]);\n  const apiModule = pathToFileURL(join(projectRoot, 'apps/api/dist/apps/api/src/index.js')).href;\n  const server = spawn(process.execPath, ['--input-type=module', '-e', `\n    import { createProductionApiServer } from ${JSON.stringify(apiModule)};\n    const server = await createProductionApiServer();\n    server.listen(0, '127.0.0.1', () => process.send({ port: server.address().port }));\n    process.once('SIGTERM', () => server.close(() => process.exit(0)));\n  `], { cwd: TARGET_FRONTEND_ROOT, stdio: ['ignore', 'ignore', 'inherit', 'ipc'], env: { ...process.env,\n    FIRST_SLICE_STORE: 'sqlite', FIRST_SLICE_SQLITE_FILE: join(root, 'owned.sqlite'),\n    FIRST_SLICE_BOOTSTRAP_DEMO: 'true', FIRST_SLICE_OPERATOR_AUTH_REQUIRED: 'true',\n    FIRST_SLICE_XML_SCHEMA_PROFILE: 'original-19', FIRST_SLICE_XML_SCHEMA_DOWNLOAD: 'false',\n    FIRST_SLICE_XML_SCHEMA_CACHE: join(projectRoot, '.data/original-xml-schemas') } });\n  let browser;\n  let page;\n  let context;\n  try {\n    const port = await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n      const timer = setTimeout(() => reject(new Error('Owned API startup timed out')), 20000);\n      server.once('message', value => { clearTimeout(timer); resolve(value.port); });\n      server.once('error', error => { clearTimeout(timer); reject(error); });\n      server.once('exit', () => { clearTimeout(timer); reject(new Error('Owned API exited before ready')); });\n    });\n    const baseUrl = 'http://127.0.0.1:' + port;\n    console.log('owned_unit_label_base_url=' + baseUrl);\n    let operatorToken;\n    const api = async (path, body, token = operatorToken) => {\n      const response = await fetch(baseUrl + path, { method: body === undefined ? 'GET' : 'POST',\n        headers: { ...(body === undefined ? {} : { 'content-type': 'application/json' }), ...(token ? { authorization: 'Bearer ' + token } : {}) },\n        ...(body === undefined ? {} : { body: JSON.stringify(body) }) });\n      const value = await response.json();\n      assert.ok(response.ok, path + ': ' + response.status + ' ' + JSON.stringify(value));\n      return value;\n    };\n    operatorToken = (await api('/api/v1/admin/auth/sign-in', { username: 'demo-admin', password: 'REDACTED' })).sessionToken;\n    if (process.env.LABEL_REPOSITORY_GATE) {\n      browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: false, channel: process.env.LABEL_BROWSER_CHANNEL || 'chrome' });\n      console.log('unit_label_browser=' + browser.version());\n      const { runParticipantUnitLabelSmoke } = await import(pathToFileURL(join(projectRoot, 'scripts/participant-unit-label-smoke.mjs')).href);\n      await runParticipantUnitLabelSmoke({ browser, baseUrl, tenantKey: 'owned-label-tenant', workspaceKey: 'owned-labels',\n        unitDocument: unit, playerDocument: player, createZip: createStoredZipBuffer, operatorToken,\n        sendJson: async (url, { body } = {}) => {\n          const response = await fetch(url, { method: 'POST', headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json', authorization: 'Bearer ' + operatorToken }, body: JSON.stringify(body) });\n          assert.ok(response.ok, url + ': ' + response.status);\n          return response;\n        } });\n      return;\n    }\n    await api('/api/v1/tenants/demo-tenant/workspaces', { workspaceKey: 'owned-labels', displayName: 'Owned short Unit label acceptance' });\n    const workspace = '/api/v1/tenants/demo-tenant/workspaces/owned-labels';\n    const uploaded = await api(workspace + '/source-packages', { fileName: 'owned-labels.zip', mediaType: 'application/zip', sourceDocument: 'data:application/zip;base64,' + archive.toString('base64') });\n    const imported = await api(workspace + '/import-jobs', { sourcePackageId: uploaded.sourcePackage.sourcePackageId });\n    assert.equal(imported.importJob.status, 'completed', JSON.stringify(imported.importJob.diagnostics));\n    assert.ok(imported.stagedContentRelease?.contentReleaseId);\n    await api(workspace + '/content-releases/' + imported.stagedContentRelease.contentReleaseId + '/activate', {});\n    await api(workspace + '/participant-roster', { rosterText: ['rewrite', 'original'].flatMap(ui => [1280, 390].flatMap(width => cases.map(item => ({\n      loginKey: 'labels-' + item.key + '-' + ui + '-' + width, groupKey: 'owned-labels', bookletKey: 'labels-' + item.key, mode: 'run-hot-return'\n    })))) });\n    browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: false, channel: process.env.LABEL_BROWSER_CHANNEL || 'chrome' });\n    console.log('unit_label_browser=' + browser.version());\n    const interfaces = process.env.LABEL_INTERFACES?.split(',') || ['rewrite', 'original'];\n    const widths = process.env.LABEL_WIDTHS?.split(',').map(Number) || [1280, 390];\n    for (const ui of interfaces) for (const width of widths) for (const item of cases.filter(item => !process.env.LABEL_CASE || item.key === process.env.LABEL_CASE)) {\n      const loginKey = 'labels-' + item.key + '-' + ui + '-' + width;\n      context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width, height: 900 } });\n      await context.tracing.start({ screenshots: true, snapshots: true, sources: true });\n      page = await context.newPage();\n      const errors = [];\n      page.on('pageerror', error => errors.push(String(error)));\n      let operatorLeaks = 0;\n      page.on('request', request => {\n        if (request.url().includes('/api/v1/participant/') && request.headers().authorization === 'Bearer ' + operatorToken) operatorLeaks++;\n      });\n      await page.goto(baseUrl + '/app/participant?' + new URLSearchParams({ ui, tenantKey: 'demo-tenant', workspaceKey: 'owned-labels' }), { waitUntil: 'networkidle' });\n      if (ui === 'original') await page.getByLabel('Anmeldename', { exact: true }).fill(loginKey);\n      else await page.locator('#participantLoginKey').fill(loginKey);\n      const signingIn = page.waitForResponse(response => new URL(response.url()).pathname === '/api/v1/participant/auth/sign-in');\n      const resuming = page.waitForResponse(response => /\\/sessions\\/[^/]+\\/resume$/.test(new URL(response.url()).pathname));\n      if (ui === 'original') await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Weiter', exact: true }).click();\n      else await page.locator('#participantRouteSignInButton').click();\n      const signedIn = await signingIn;\n      assert.equal(signedIn.status(), 200);\n      const identity = await signedIn.json();\n      assert.notEqual(identity.sessionToken, operatorToken);\n      // A single assigned saving Booklet starts through the real automatic\n      // participant-entry workflow. Observe its request before submitting login.\n      const resumed = await resuming;\n      assert.equal(resumed.status(), 200);\n      const runId = (await resumed.json()).testRun.testRunId;\n      const state = () => api('/api/v1/participant/sessions/' + identity.participantSession.participantSessionId + '/current-state?testRunId=' + runId, undefined, identity.sessionToken);\n      await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerVersion').filter({ hasText: 'API 6.0' }).waitFor({ state: ui === 'original' ? 'attached' : 'visible' });\n      const assertLabels = async (full, short, position) => {\n        const waitText = (selector, expected) => page.waitForFunction(({ selector, expected }) =>\n          document.querySelector(selector)?.textContent?.trim().replace(/\\s+/g, ' ') === expected, { selector, expected });\n        await page.waitForFunction(expected => document.querySelector('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame')?.getAttribute('title') === expected, full);\n        const chosen = mode => mode === 'short' ? short || full : mode === 'booklet' ? 'Label booklet ' + item.key : full;\n        const headerSelector = ui === 'original' ? '#participantApplicationHeader h1' : '#participantRouteScreenHeader';\n        const header = page.locator(headerSelector);\n        await waitText(headerSelector, chosen(item.header));\n        assert.equal((await header.textContent()).trim(), chosen(item.header));\n        const toolbarSelector = ui === 'original' ? '#originalPlayerToolbar [data-cy=\"unit-title\"]' : '#participantRouteUnit';\n        const toolbar = page.locator(toolbarSelector);\n        if (item.toolbar === 'hidden') assert.equal(await toolbar.count(), 0);\n        else { await waitText(toolbarSelector, chosen(item.toolbar)); assert.equal((await toolbar.textContent()).trim(), chosen(item.toolbar)); }\n        const navigation = page.locator(ui === 'original' ? '#originalUnitNavigation-label' : '#participantRouteUnitNavigationLabel');\n        if (item.nav === 'hidden') assert.equal(await navigation.count(), 0);\n        else {\n          const expected = item.nav === 'index' ? (ui === 'original' ? 'Aufgabe ' + position + '/2' : 'Unit ' + position + ' / 2') : chosen(item.nav);\n          await waitText(ui === 'original' ? '#originalUnitNavigation-label' : '#participantRouteUnitNavigationLabel', expected);\n          assert.equal((await navigation.textContent()).trim().replace(/\\s+/g, ' '), expected);\n        }\n        assert.equal(await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').getAttribute('title'), full);\n      };\n      await assertLabels(fullA, shortA, 1);\n      const firstState = await state();\n      assert.equal(firstState.currentRunState.bookletUnits[0].shortLabel, shortA);\n      assert.equal(firstState.currentRunState.bookletUnits[1].shortLabel, undefined);\n      await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').scrollIntoViewIfNeeded();\n      await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').screenshot();\n      const radio = page.frameLocator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').locator('[data-cy=\"TestController-radio1-Aufg1\"]');\n      if (process.env.LABEL_DIAGNOSTICS) {\n        console.log('unit_label_geometry=' + JSON.stringify({ ui, width, key: item.key,\n          owner: await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').boundingBox(),\n          radio: await radio.boundingBox(),\n          inner: await radio.evaluate(element => ({ width: innerWidth, height: innerHeight, scrollX, scrollY,\n            box: element.getBoundingClientRect().toJSON(), checked: element.checked,\n            hit: document.elementFromPoint(element.getBoundingClientRect().x + element.getBoundingClientRect().width / 2,\n              element.getBoundingClientRect().y + element.getBoundingClientRect().height / 2)?.outerHTML.slice(0, 300) })) }));\n      }\n      await radio.check();\n      let saved;\n      for (let attempt = 0; attempt < 100; attempt++) {\n        const snapshot = await state();\n        const raw = snapshot.currentRunState.testRun.unitResponses.a;\n        if (raw && JSON.parse(raw).unitState?.dataParts?.answers?.includes('VALUE_CHANGED')) { saved = raw; break; }\n        await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 100));\n      }\n      assert.ok(saved, 'Native radio answer must be durably saved');\n      await page.locator(ui === 'original' ? '#participantVeronaGlobalForwardButton' : '#participantRouteNextUnitButton').click();\n      await assertLabels(fullB, undefined, 2);\n      await page.locator(ui === 'original' ? '#participantVeronaGlobalBackwardButton' : '#participantRoutePreviousUnitButton').click();\n      await assertLabels(fullA, shortA, 1);\n      assert.equal((await state()).currentRunState.testRun.unitResponses.a, saved);\n      await page.reload({ waitUntil: 'networkidle' });\n      await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerVersion').filter({ hasText: 'API 6.0' }).waitFor({ state: ui === 'original' ? 'attached' : 'visible' });\n      await assertLabels(fullA, shortA, 1);\n      assert.equal((await state()).currentRunState.testRun.testRunId, runId);\n      assert.equal((await state()).currentRunState.testRun.unitResponses.a, saved);\n      assert.equal(await page.frameLocator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').locator('[data-cy=\"TestController-radio1-Aufg1\"]').isChecked(), true);\n      assert.equal(operatorLeaks, 0);\n      assert.deepEqual(errors, []);\n      await page.screenshot({ path: join(root, ui + '-' + width + '-' + item.key + '.png'), fullPage: true });\n      await context.tracing.stop({ path: join(root, ui + '-' + width + '-' + item.key + '.zip') });\n      await context.close();\n      context = null;\n      console.log('unit_labels=' + ui + '/' + width + '/' + item.key + ':passed');\n    }\n    console.log('unit_labels_all_selected_cases_passed=true');\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (page) await page.screenshot({ path: join(root, 'failure.png'), fullPage: true }).catch(() => {});\n    if (context) await context.tracing.stop({ path: join(root, 'failure.zip') }).catch(() => {});\n    throw error;\n  } finally {\n    await browser?.close();\n    const exited = new Promise(resolve => server.once('exit', resolve));\n    server.kill('SIGTERM');\n    await Promise.race([exited, new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 5000))]);\n    if (server.exitCode === null) server.kill('SIGKILL');\n  }\n})().catch(error => { console.error('unit_label_browser_error=' + error.message); process.exitCode = 1; });\n"},"started_at_ms":1791437819230,"completed_at_ms":1791437819230}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-08T05:36:59.286Z","ordinal":95146,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a","turn_id":"01a1199d-3152-75c1-89b7-3e60b92f4af5","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-9b178e15-06bd-46c5-b1d4-8a44c980c167","process_id":"7695","command":["/bin/zsh","-c","git log origin/master -6 --oneline"],"cwd":"file:///Users/julian/code/testcenter","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git log origin/master -6 --oneline"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"14c982845 [fe] Show unit short label in header, navbar and toolbar\ndfb7c72f3 [fe] Show toolbar text and icons in on-primary colour\n6b1adeb05 [be] Test that TestDAO rejects log arrays of the wrong type\n414fe6b80 [be] Remove unused imports and fix UploadedFile annotation\n1caf54eb2 [be][infra] Run Mago from a pinned binary in the dev container\n4b9a1e7f4 Merge pull request #1624 from iqb-berlin/fix/resolve-type-errors\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"14c982845 [fe] Show unit short label in header, navbar and toolbar\ndfb7c72f3 [fe] Show toolbar text and icons in on-primary colour\n6b1adeb05 [be] Test that TestDAO rejects log arrays of the wrong type\n414fe6b80 [be] Remove unused imports and fix UploadedFile annotation\n1caf54eb2 [be][infra] Run Mago from a pinned binary in the dev container\n4b9a1e7f4 Merge pull request #1624 from iqb-berlin/fix/resolve-type-errors\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":7333},"formatted_output":"14c982845 [fe] Show unit short label in header, navbar and toolbar\ndfb7c72f3 [fe] Show toolbar text and icons in on-primary colour\n6b1adeb05 [be] Test that TestDAO rejects log arrays of the wrong type\n414fe6b80 [be] Remove unused imports and fix UploadedFile annotation\n1caf54eb2 [be][infra] Run Mago from a pinned binary in the dev container\n4b9a1e7f4 Merge pull request #1624 from iqb-berlin/fix/resolve-type-errors\n"},"started_at_ms":1791437819286,"completed_at_ms":1791437819286}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-08T05:36:59.338Z","ordinal":95147,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a","turn_id":"01a1199d-3152-75c1-89b7-3e60b92f4af5","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3e6f4081-aa79-4639-b374-415d244d8f14","process_id":"29916","command":["/bin/zsh","-c","rg '^ui_smoke_step=|^actual_native_whole_error=|^native-controller-event=' /tmp/testcenter-controller-native-whole-20261008.log | tail -12"],"cwd":"file:///Users/julian/Documents/Codex/2026-08-13/arbeite-im-repo-users-julian-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg '^ui_smoke_step=|''^actual_native_whole_error=|''^native-controller-event=' /tmp/testcenter-controller-native-whole-20261008.log","query":"^ui_smoke_step=|^actual_native_whole_error=|^native-controller-event=","path":"testcenter-controller-native-whole-20261008.log"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"ui_smoke_step=action-sign-out-start\nui_smoke_step=action-sign-out-done\nui_smoke_step=action-sign-in-start\nui_smoke_step=action-sign-in-done\nui_smoke_step=action-admin-sessions-start\nui_smoke_step=action-admin-sessions-done\nui_smoke_step=admin-session-bulk-revoke\nui_smoke_step=action-admin-users-start\nui_smoke_step=action-admin-users-done\nui_smoke_step=admin-user-bulk-password\nui_smoke_step=admin-user-bulk-role\nui_smoke_step=admin-user-bulk-status\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"ui_smoke_step=action-sign-out-start\nui_smoke_step=action-sign-out-done\nui_smoke_step=action-sign-in-start\nui_smoke_step=action-sign-in-done\nui_smoke_step=action-admin-sessions-start\nui_smoke_step=action-admin-sessions-done\nui_smoke_step=admin-session-bulk-revoke\nui_smoke_step=action-admin-users-start\nui_smoke_step=action-admin-users-done\nui_smoke_step=admin-user-bulk-password\nui_smoke_step=admin-user-bulk-role\nui_smoke_step=admin-user-bulk-status\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":8208},"formatted_output":"ui_smoke_step=action-sign-out-start\nui_smoke_step=action-sign-out-done\nui_smoke_step=action-sign-in-start\nui_smoke_step=action-sign-in-done\nui_smoke_step=action-admin-sessions-start\nui_smoke_step=action-admin-sessions-done\nui_smoke_step=admin-session-bulk-revoke\nui_smoke_step=action-admin-users-start\nui_smoke_step=action-admin-users-done\nui_smoke_step=admin-user-bulk-password\nui_smoke_step=admin-user-bulk-role\nui_smoke_step=admin-user-bulk-status\n"},"started_at_ms":1791437819338,"completed_at_ms":1791437819338}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-08T05:36:59.343Z","ordinal":95148,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a11a03-cdcf-7aa2-ba33-3355f4f8c660","call_id":"call_dad0ef175df34c76ab76783d5f1b8745","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"7fc35c\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000010375,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1102,\"output\":\"The unchanged `68c883b9` complete protected SQLite/production Chrome sequence\\nfails at the later saved-QR-image Attachment Capture step, before group deletion.\\nAn isolated actual attachment smoke repeats the same missing-target timeout;\\nthe rendered UI reports a scanner timeout and makes no successful target lookup.\\nIt is not a complete-flow pass or evidence that short Unit labels caused the\\nfailure. The precise QR-decoder cause, PostgreSQL snapshot/count failure,\\ncomplete-flow CI, all eight full Original-UI rows and broader production\\nacceptance remain open. This step is not a 100-percent or merge-ready claim.\\n\\n### Current independent short Unit labels (2026-10-08)\\n\\nThe upstream target remains `14c98284590195631750bb2352cb398ca669fe7d`,\\nindependently reverified against remote `master` on 2026-10-08. Actual source\\nconfiguration defaults the header to the Booklet label, navigation to the Unit\\nindex and toolbar to the full Unit label. Header `UNIT_LABEL_SHORT`, navigation\\n`LABEL_SHORT` and toolbar `LABEL_SHORT` now compile and render independently.\\nAbsent or empty `labelshort` falls back to the selected Unit's full label.\\nModern `toolbar_unit_label` takes precedence by key presence, followed by\\n`toolbar_show_unit_title` and then older `unit_title`; explicit newer empty keys\\ndo not fall through to older values. `HIDDEN` remains a rendering decision,\\nnot an authorization or Player-metadata change.\\n\\nOlder immutable snapshots project their previously unsupported short-label\\nsource keys when read. Explicit historical values without those source keys,\\nincluding a hidden header/title, remain unchanged. This does not rewrite a\\nrelease, create/reset a Run, replace a saved answer or alter navigation locks.\\nThe actual facade's Verona `unitTitle` and iframe title remain the full label;\\nthe visual navigation label does not remount or reconfigure the Player.\\n\\nFour compiler and twelve actual-facade/projection/corpus regressions run in\\nthe normal test commands. All 432 core/frontend checks, typecheck and the\\nproduction build pass. All 164 API tests pass separately in memory, file and\\nSQLite (492 total). The official historical corpus's literal policy expectations\\nadd only the new toolbar mode; its other exact assertions and vendor bytes are\\nunchanged. The production initial bundle is 469.98 kB, still under the unchanged\\n470-kB error budget; its existing warning thresholds are not raised.\\n\\nThe new `participant-current-unit-labels` section of the complete repository\\nbrowser smoke uses seven checked-in, source-derived configurations and native\\nBooklet 18.0 XML with aliases of the unchanged pinned Controller Unit/Player.\\nIt performs real UI login in fresh contexts, independent exact labels, a\\nmissing-short-label second Unit, trusted native radio input, forward/backward\\nnavigation, exact durable answer and same-Run hard reload. Its owned strict\\nOriginal-19/immutable-production Chrome 154 run passes all 28 combinations\\n(seven configurations, both interfaces, 1280/390 widths). Operator credential\\nleaks and browser page errors must be zero. Bundled Chromium 147 independently\\npasses the same 28 cases on its own fixture (56 browser cases total). The newly\\nextended whole sequence and fresh publication CI are separate checks.\\n\\nThe initial mobile Rewrite repetition fails because its nested cards shrink\\nthe unchanged Player to 280 pixels while the vendor reserves `9em` on each\\nside. The native radio is clipped behind the form's hit target. Original's\\n390-pixel surface passes the same real input. Only mobile Rewrite Player/card\\npadding is reduced; the final seven mobile Rewrite cases pass without forced\\nclicks, synthetic events, added retry loops, vendor/CSS injection or sandbox changes.\\n\\nThe preceding unchanged `5e69fb1d` complete protected SQLite/production Chrome\\nsequence also passes through monitor, exports and teardown. It is not proof\\nof these new label changes. That publication still has a remote PostgreSQL UI\\nfailure: group deletion reports 45 logs against a previously captured 44-log\\nsnapshot. Its cause and exact deletion evidence remain to be resolved; local\\nSQLite success is not PostgreSQL or merge acceptance. Toolbar on-primary\\ncolors, all eight full-page Original-UI rows and broader production acceptance\\nremain open. This step is not a 100-percent or merge-ready claim.\\n\\n### Original Controller native input after viewport rendering (2026-10-08)\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"794d97\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007667,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":4135,\"output\":\"const TARGET_FRONTEND_ROOT = process.env.TARGET_FRONTEND_ROOT;\\nif (!TARGET_FRONTEND_ROOT) throw new Error('Immutable production frontend required.');\\n(async () => {\\n  const assert = require('node:assert/strict');\\n  const { spawn } = require('node:child_process');\\n  const fs = require('node:fs/promises');\\n  const { join } = require('node:path');\\n  const { tmpdir } = require('node:os');\\n  const { pathToFileURL } = require('node:url');\\n  const { brotliDecompressSync } = require('node:zlib');\\n  const { chromium } = require('playwright');\\n  const projectRoot = '/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app';\\n  const ts = require(require.resolve('typescript', { paths: [projectRoot] }));\\n  process.chdir(projectRoot);\\n  const root = await fs.mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), 'testcenter-short-labels-browser-'));\\n  console.log('owned_unit_label_artifacts=' + root);\\n  const source = await fs.readFile(join(projectRoot, 'scripts/smoke-ui.mjs'), 'utf8');\\n  const ast = ts.createSourceFile('smoke-ui.mjs', source, ts.ScriptTarget.ES2022, true, ts.ScriptKind.JS);\\n  const zipNames = ['crc32Table', 'crc32', 'createStoredZipBuffer'];\\n  const zipDeclarations = [];\\n  const visit = node => {\\n    if (ts.isVariableDeclaration(node) && zipNames.includes(node.name.getText(ast))) zipDeclarations.push(node.getText(ast));\\n    ts.forEachChild(node, visit);\\n  };\\n  visit(ast);\\n  assert.equal(zipDeclarations.length, zipNames.length);\\n  const { createStoredZipBuffer } = await import('data:text/javascript;base64,' + Buffer.from(\\n    zipDeclarations.map(text => 'const ' + text + ';').join('\\\\n') + '\\\\nexport { createStoredZipBuffer };').toString('base64'));\\n  const corpusRoot = join(projectRoot, 'test-fixtures/original-testcenter');\\n  const corpus = JSON.parse(await fs.readFile(join(corpusRoot, 'corpus.json'), 'utf8'));\\n  const official = corpus.currentOriginalTestControllerPackage;\\n  const unitFixture = official.units.find(item => item[1] === 'CY-Unit.Sample-101');\\n  const unit = Buffer.from((await fs.readFile(join(corpusRoot, unitFixture[0]), 'utf8')).trim(), 'base64').toString('utf8');\\n  const player = brotliDecompressSync(Buffer.from(await fs.readFile(join(corpusRoot, official.player.fixture), 'utf8'), 'base64')).toString('utf8');\\n  const { cases } = JSON.parse(await fs.readFile(join(corpusRoot, 'current-unit-label-cases.json'), 'utf8'));\\n  const xmlEscape = value => value.replaceAll('&', '&amp;').replaceAll('\\\"', '&quot;').replaceAll('<', '&lt;');\\n  const fullA = 'Volle Aufgabe ä/β';\\n  const fullB = 'Zweite volle Aufgabe ä/β';\\n  const shortA = 'Kurz ä/β';\\n  const booklets = cases.map(item => ({ fileName: 'booklets/' + item.key + '.xml', content:\\n    '<?xml version=\\\"1.0\\\"?><Booklet xmlns:xsi=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\\\" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation=\\\"https://w3id.org/iqb/spec/testcenter-booklet-xml/18.0\\\">' +\\n    '<Metadata><Id>labels-' + item.key + '</Id><Label>Label booklet ' + item.key + '</Label></Metadata><BookletConfig>' +\\n    Object.entries({ pagingMode: 'buttons', navbar_forward_button: 'UNITS', navbar_backward_button: 'UNITS', unit_responses_buffer_time: '0', ...item.config })\\n      .map(([key, value]) => '<Config key=\\\"' + key + '\\\">' + xmlEscape(value) + '</Config>').join('') +\\n    '</BookletConfig><Units><Testlet id=\\\"owned-block\\\" label=\\\"Owned block\\\"><Unit id=\\\"CY-Unit.Sample-101\\\" alias=\\\"a\\\" label=\\\"' + fullA + '\\\" labelshort=\\\"' + shortA + '\\\"/>' +\\n    '<Unit id=\\\"CY-Unit.Sample-101\\\" alias=\\\"b\\\" label=\\\"' + fullB + '\\\"/></Testlet></Units></Booklet>' }));\\n  const archive = createStoredZipBuffer([...booklets, { fileName: 'units/CY_Unit101.xml', content: unit },\\n    { fileName: 'players/verona-player-simple-6.0.html', content: player }]);\\n  const apiModule = pathToFileURL(join(projectRoot, 'apps/api/dist/apps/api/src/index.js')).href;\\n  const server = spawn(process.execPath, ['--input-type=module', '-e', `\\n    import { createProductionApiServer } from ${JSON.stringify(apiModule)};\\n    const server = await createProductionApiServer();\\n    server.listen(0, '127.0.0.1', () => process.send({ port: server.address().port }));\\n    process.once('SIGTERM', () => server.close(() => process.exit(0)));\\n  `], { cwd: TARGET_FRONTEND_ROOT, stdio: ['ignore', 'ignore', 'inherit', 'ipc'], env: { ...process.env,\\n    FIRST_SLICE_STORE: 'sqlite', FIRST_SLICE_SQLITE_FILE: join(root, 'owned.sqlite'),\\n    FIRST_SLICE_BOOTSTRAP_DEMO: 'true', FIRST_SLICE_OPERATOR_AUTH_REQUIRED: 'true',\\n    FIRST_SLICE_XML_SCHEMA_PROFILE: 'original-19', FIRST_SLICE_XML_SCHEMA_DOWNLOAD: 'false',\\n    FIRST_SLICE_XML_SCHEMA_CACHE: join(projectRoot, '.data/original-xml-schemas') } });\\n  let browser;\\n  let page;\\n  let context;\\n  try {\\n    const port = await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\\n      const timer = setTimeout(() => reject(new Error('Owned API startup timed out')), 20000);\\n      server.once('message', value => { clearTimeout(timer); resolve(value.port); });\\n      server.once('error', error => { clearTimeout(timer); reject(error); });\\n      server.once('exit', () => { clearTimeout(timer); reject(new Error('Owned API exited before ready')); });\\n    });\\n    const baseUrl = 'http://127.0.0.1:' + port;\\n    console.log('owned_unit_label_base_url=' + baseUrl);\\n    let operatorToken;\\n    const api = async (path, body, token = operatorToken) => {\\n      const response = await fetch(baseUrl + path, { method: body === undefined ? 'GET' : 'POST',\\n        headers: { ...(body === undefined ? {} : { 'content-type': 'application/json' }), ...(token ? { authorization: 'Bearer ' + token } : {}) },\\n        ...(body === undefined ? {} : { body: JSON.stringify(body) }) });\\n      const value = await response.json();\\n      assert.ok(response.ok, path + ': ' + response.status + ' ' + JSON.stringify(value));\\n      return value;\\n    };\\n    operatorToken = (await api('/api/v1/admin/auth/sign-in', { username: 'demo-admin', password: 'REDACTED' })).sessionToken;\\n    if (process.env.LABEL_REPOSITORY_GATE) {\\n      browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: false, channel: process.env.LABEL_BROWSER_CHANNEL || 'chrome' });\\n      console.log('unit_label_browser=' + browser.version());\\n      const { runParticipantUnitLabelSmoke } = await import(pathToFileURL(join(projectRoot, 'scripts/participant-unit-label-smoke.mjs')).href);\\n      await runParticipantUnitLabelSmoke({ browser, baseUrl, tenantKey: 'owned-label-tenant', workspaceKey: 'owned-labels',\\n        unitDocument: unit, playerDocument: player, createZip: createStoredZipBuffer, operatorToken,\\n        sendJson: async (url, { body } = {}) => {\\n          const response = await fetch(url, { method: 'POST', headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json', authorization: 'Bearer ' + operatorToken }, body: JSON.stringify(body) });\\n          assert.ok(response.ok, url + ': ' + response.status);\\n          return response;\\n        } });\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    await api('/api/v1/tenants/demo-tenant/workspaces', { workspaceKey: 'owned-labels', displayName: 'Owned short Unit label acceptance' });\\n    const workspace = '/api/v1/tenants/demo-tenant/workspaces/owned-labels';\\n    const uploaded = await api(workspace + '/source-packages', { fileName: 'owned-labels.zip', mediaType: 'application/zip', sourceDocument: 'data:application/zip;base64,' + archive.toString('base64') });\\n    const imported = await api(workspace + '/import-jobs', { sourcePackageId: uploaded.sourcePackage.sourcePackageId });\\n    assert.equal(imported.importJob.status, 'completed', JSON.stringify(imported.importJob.diagnostics));\\n    assert.ok(imported.stagedContentRelease?.contentReleaseId);\\n    await api(workspace + '/content-releases/' + imported.stagedContentRelease.contentReleaseId + '/activate', {});\\n    await api(workspace + '/participant-roster', { rosterText: ['rewrite', 'original'].flatMap(ui => [1280, 390].flatMap(width => cases.map(item => ({\\n      loginKey: 'labels-' + item.key + '-' + ui + '-' + width, groupKey: 'owned-labels', bookletKey: 'labels-' + item.key, mode: 'run-hot-return'\\n    })))) });\\n    browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: false, channel: process.env.LABEL_BROWSER_CHANNEL || 'chrome' });\\n    console.log('unit_label_browser=' + browser.version());\\n    const interfaces = process.env.LABEL_INTERFACES?.split(',') || ['rewrite', 'original'];\\n    const widths = process.env.LABEL_WIDTHS?.split(',').map(Number) || [1280, 390];\\n    for (const ui of interfaces) for (const width of widths) for (const item of cases.filter(item => !process.env.LABEL_CASE || item.key === process.env.LABEL_CASE)) {\\n      const loginKey = 'labels-' + item.key + '-' + ui + '-' + width;\\n      context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width, height: 900 } });\\n      await context.tracing.start({ screenshots: true, snapshots: true, sources: true });\\n      page = await context.newPage();\\n      const errors = [];\\n      page.on('pageerror', error => errors.push(String(error)));\\n      let operatorLeaks = 0;\\n      page.on('request', request => {\\n        if (request.url().includes('/api/v1/participant/') && request.headers().authorization === 'Bearer ' + operatorToken) operatorLeaks++;\\n      });\\n      await page.goto(baseUrl + '/app/participant?' + new URLSearchParams({ ui, tenantKey: 'demo-tenant', workspaceKey: 'owned-labels' }), { waitUntil: 'networkidle' });\\n      if (ui === 'original') await page.getByLabel('Anmeldename', { exact: true }).fill(loginKey);\\n      else await page.locator('#participantLoginKey').fill(loginKey);\\n      const signingIn = page.waitForResponse(response => new URL(response.url()).pathname === '/api/v1/participant/auth/sign-in');\\n      const resuming = page.waitForResponse(response => /\\\\/sessions\\\\/[^/]+\\\\/resume$/.test(new URL(response.url()).pathname));\\n      if (ui === 'original') await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Weiter', exact: true }).click();\\n      else await page.locator('#participantRouteSignInButton').click();\\n      const signedIn = await signingIn;\\n      assert.equal(signedIn.status(), 200);\\n      const identity = await signedIn.json();\\n      assert.notEqual(identity.sessionToken, operatorToken);\\n      // A single assigned saving Booklet starts through the real automatic\\n      // participant-entry workflow. Observe its request before submitting login.\\n      const resumed = await resuming;\\n      assert.equal(resumed.status(), 200);\\n      const runId = (await resumed.json()).testRun.testRunId;\\n      const state = () => api('/api/v1/participant/sessions/' + identity.participantSession.participantSessionId + '/current-state?testRunId=' + runId, undefined, identity.sessionToken);\\n      await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerVersion').filter({ hasText: 'API 6.0' }).waitFor({ state: ui === 'original' ? 'attached' : 'visible' });\\n      const assertLabels = async (full, short, position) => {\\n        const waitText = (selector, expected) => page.waitForFunction(({ selector, expected }) =>\\n          document.querySelector(selector)?.textContent?.trim().replace(/\\\\s+/g, ' ') === expected, { selector, expected });\\n        await page.waitForFunction(expected => document.querySelector('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame')?.getAttribute('title') === expected, full);\\n        const chosen = mode => mode === 'short' ? short || full : mode === 'booklet' ? 'Label booklet ' + item.key : full;\\n        const headerSelector = ui === 'original' ? '#participantApplicationHeader h1' : '#participantRouteScreenHeader';\\n        const header = page.locator(headerSelector);\\n        await waitText(headerSelector, chosen(item.header));\\n        assert.equal((await header.textContent()).trim(), chosen(item.header));\\n        const toolbarSelector = ui === 'original' ? '#originalPlayerToolbar [data-cy=\\\"unit-title\\\"]' : '#participantRouteUnit';\\n        const toolbar = page.locator(toolbarSelector);\\n        if (item.toolbar === 'hidden') assert.equal(await toolbar.count(), 0);\\n        else { await waitText(toolbarSelector, chosen(item.toolbar)); assert.equal((await toolbar.textContent()).trim(), chosen(item.toolbar)); }\\n        const navigation = page.locator(ui === 'original' ? '#originalUnitNavigation-label' : '#participantRouteUnitNavigationLabel');\\n        if (item.nav === 'hidden') assert.equal(await navigation.count(), 0);\\n        else {\\n          const expected = item.nav === 'index' ? (ui === 'original' ? 'Aufgabe ' + position + '/2' : 'Unit ' + position + ' / 2') : chosen(item.nav);\\n          await waitText(ui === 'original' ? '#originalUnitNavigation-label' : '#participantRouteUnitNavigationLabel', expected);\\n          assert.equal((await navigation.textContent()).trim().replace(/\\\\s+/g, ' '), expected);\\n        }\\n        assert.equal(await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').getAttribute('title'), full);\\n      };\\n      await assertLabels(fullA, shortA, 1);\\n      const firstState = await state();\\n      assert.equal(firstState.currentRunState.bookletUnits[0].shortLabel, shortA);\\n      assert.equal(firstState.currentRunState.bookletUnits[1].shortLabel, undefined);\\n      await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').scrollIntoViewIfNeeded();\\n      await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').screenshot();\\n      const radio = page.frameLocator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').locator('[data-cy=\\\"TestController-radio1-Aufg1\\\"]');\\n      if (process.env.LABEL_DIAGNOSTICS) {\\n        console.log('unit_label_geometry=' + JSON.stringify({ ui, width, key: item.key,\\n          owner: await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').boundingBox(),\\n          radio: await radio.boundingBox(),\\n          inner: await radio.evaluate(element => ({ width: innerWidth, height: innerHeight, scrollX, scrollY,\\n            box: element.getBoundingClientRect().toJSON(), checked: element.checked,\\n            hit: document.elementFromPoint(element.getBoundingClientRect().x + element.getBoundingClientRect().width / 2,\\n              element.getBoundingClientRect().y + element.getBoundingClientRect().height / 2)?.outerHTML.slice(0, 300) })) }));\\n      }\\n      await radio.check();\\n      let saved;\\n      for (let attempt = 0; attempt < 100; attempt++) {\\n        const snapshot = await state();\\n        const raw = snapshot.currentRunState.testRun.unitResponses.a;\\n        if (raw && JSON.parse(raw).unitState?.dataParts?.answers?.includes('VALUE_CHANGED')) { saved = raw; break; }\\n        await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 100));\\n      }\\n      assert.ok(saved, 'Native radio answer must be durably saved');\\n      await page.locator(ui === 'original' ? '#participantVeronaGlobalForwardButton' : '#participantRouteNextUnitButton').click();\\n      await assertLabels(fullB, undefined, 2);\\n      await page.locator(ui === 'original' ? '#participantVeronaGlobalBackwardButton' : '#participantRoutePreviousUnitButton').click();\\n      await assertLabels(fullA, shortA, 1);\\n      assert.equal((await state()).currentRunState.testRun.unitResponses.a, saved);\\n      await page.reload({ waitUntil: 'networkidle' });\\n      await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerVersion').filter({ hasText: 'API 6.0' }).waitFor({ state: ui === 'original' ? 'attached' : 'visible' });\\n      await assertLabels(fullA, shortA, 1);\\n      assert.equal((await state()).currentRunState.testRun.testRunId, runId);\\n      assert.equal((await state()).currentRunState.testRun.unitResponses.a, saved);\\n      assert.equal(await page.frameLocator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').locator('[data-cy=\\\"TestController-radio1-Aufg1\\\"]').isChecked(), true);\\n      assert.equal(operatorLeaks, 0);\\n      assert.deepEqual(errors, []);\\n      await page.screenshot({ path: join(root, ui + '-' + width + '-' + item.key + '.png'), fullPage: true });\\n      await context.tracing.stop({ path: join(root, ui + '-' + width + '-' + item.key + '.zip') });\\n      await context.close();\\n      context = null;\\n      console.log('unit_labels=' + ui + '/' + width + '/' + item.key + ':passed');\\n    }\\n    console.log('unit_labels_all_selected_cases_passed=true');\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    if (page) await page.screenshot({ path: join(root, 'failure.png'), fullPage: true }).catch(() => {});\\n    if (context) await context.tracing.stop({ path: join(root, 'failure.zip') }).catch(() => {});\\n    throw error;\\n  } finally {\\n    await browser?.close();\\n    const exited = new Promise(resolve => server.once('exit', resolve));\\n    server.kill('SIGTERM');\\n    await Promise.race([exited, new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 5000))]);\\n    if (server.exitCode === null) server.kill('SIGKILL');\\n  }\\n})().catch(error => { console.error('unit_label_browser_error=' + error.message); process.exitCode = 1; });\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"12ac4f\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007333,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":105,\"output\":\"14c982845 [fe] Show unit short label in header, navbar and toolbar\\ndfb7c72f3 [fe] Show toolbar text and icons in on-primary colour\\n6b1adeb05 [be] Test that TestDAO rejects log arrays of the wrong type\\n414fe6b80 [be] Remove unused imports and fix UploadedFile annotation\\n1caf54eb2 [be][infra] Run Mago from a pinned binary in the dev container\\n4b9a1e7f4 Merge pull request #1624 from iqb-berlin/fix/resolve-type-errors\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"8b1ecd\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000008208,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":113,\"output\":\"ui_smoke_step=action-sign-out-start\\nui_smoke_step=action-sign-out-done\\nui_smoke_step=action-sign-in-start\\nui_smoke_step=action-sign-in-done\\nui_smoke_step=action-admin-sessions-start\\nui_smoke_step=action-admin-sessions-done\\nui_smoke_step=admin-session-bulk-revoke\\nui_smoke_step=action-admin-users-start\\nui_smoke_step=action-admin-users-done\\nui_smoke_step=admin-user-bulk-password\\nui_smoke_step=admin-user-bulk-role\\nui_smoke_step=admin-user-bulk-status\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1199d-3152-75c1-89b7-3e60b92f4af5","create_time":1791437819.343791}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
