{"timestamp":"2026-10-08T05:47:49.887Z","ordinal":95429,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a","turn_id":"01a1199d-3152-75c1-89b7-3e60b92f4af5","session_id":"01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a","root_turn_id":"01a1199d-3152-75c1-89b7-3e60b92f4af5","response_id":"resp_06ef5e23f2db4ce4016ac72e7207a88191836dd149b75d0bde","usage":{"input_tokens":231068,"cached_input_tokens":228992,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":855,"reasoning_output_tokens":298,"total_tokens":231923},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":7774362,"cached_input_tokens":7623808,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":28457,"reasoning_output_tokens":12758,"total_tokens":7802819},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":826545199,"cached_input_tokens":804530688,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3521034,"reasoning_output_tokens":1460963,"total_tokens":830066233}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-08T05:47:51.025Z","ordinal":95430,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a","turn_id":"01a1199d-3152-75c1-89b7-3e60b92f4af5","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3a32b20a-88f3-4a11-b439-0f9336b32b3f","process_id":"65825","command":["/bin/zsh","-c","entire session attach --help"],"cwd":"file:///Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"entire session attach --help"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"Attach an existing agent session that wasn't captured by hooks.\n\nThis creates a checkpoint from the session's transcript and links it to the\nlast commit. Use this when hooks failed to fire or weren't installed when\nthe session started, or to attach a research session.\n\nIf the last commit already has a checkpoint, the session is added to it.\nOtherwise a new checkpoint is created.\n\nUse --review to tag the attached session as an agent review. The\nfirst user prompt in the transcript is recorded as the review prompt.\nPass --skills to declare which skills were actually run; omit to\nattach a review without a declared skills list.\n\nWorks with any registered agent, including external agents enabled via\nexternal_agents in settings. Run 'entire agent list' to see the full list.\n\nIf --agent doesn't locate a transcript, Entire auto-detects the agent from\nthe transcript and prints the detected agent name.\n\nUsage:\n  entire session attach <session-id> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -a, --agent string     Agent that created the session (see 'entire agent list' for registered agents, including external) (default \"claude-code\")\n  -f, --force            Skip confirmation and amend the last commit with the checkpoint trailer (best-effort; if the amend fails the checkpoint is still created and the trailer is printed for manual paste)\n  -h, --help             help for attach\n      --review           Tag the attached session as an agent review\n      --skills strings   Optional: declare which review skills were run in this session. Only used with --review\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"Attach an existing agent session that wasn't captured by hooks.\n\nThis creates a checkpoint from the session's transcript and links it to the\nlast commit. Use this when hooks failed to fire or weren't installed when\nthe session started, or to attach a research session.\n\nIf the last commit already has a checkpoint, the session is added to it.\nOtherwise a new checkpoint is created.\n\nUse --review to tag the attached session as an agent review. The\nfirst user prompt in the transcript is recorded as the review prompt.\nPass --skills to declare which skills were actually run; omit to\nattach a review without a declared skills list.\n\nWorks with any registered agent, including external agents enabled via\nexternal_agents in settings. Run 'entire agent list' to see the full list.\n\nIf --agent doesn't locate a transcript, Entire auto-detects the agent from\nthe transcript and prints the detected agent name.\n\nUsage:\n  entire session attach <session-id> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -a, --agent string     Agent that created the session (see 'entire agent list' for registered agents, including external) (default \"claude-code\")\n  -f, --force            Skip confirmation and amend the last commit with the checkpoint trailer (best-effort; if the amend fails the checkpoint is still created and the trailer is printed for manual paste)\n  -h, --help             help for attach\n      --review           Tag the attached session as an agent review\n      --skills strings   Optional: declare which review skills were run in this session. Only used with --review\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":7792},"formatted_output":"Attach an existing agent session that wasn't captured by hooks.\n\nThis creates a checkpoint from the session's transcript and links it to the\nlast commit. Use this when hooks failed to fire or weren't installed when\nthe session started, or to attach a research session.\n\nIf the last commit already has a checkpoint, the session is added to it.\nOtherwise a new checkpoint is created.\n\nUse --review to tag the attached session as an agent review. The\nfirst user prompt in the transcript is recorded as the review prompt.\nPass --skills to declare which skills were actually run; omit to\nattach a review without a declared skills list.\n\nWorks with any registered agent, including external agents enabled via\nexternal_agents in settings. Run 'entire agent list' to see the full list.\n\nIf --agent doesn't locate a transcript, Entire auto-detects the agent from\nthe transcript and prints the detected agent name.\n\nUsage:\n  entire session attach <session-id> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -a, --agent string     Agent that created the session (see 'entire agent list' for registered agents, including external) (default \"claude-code\")\n  -f, --force            Skip confirmation and amend the last commit with the checkpoint trailer (best-effort; if the amend fails the checkpoint is still created and the trailer is printed for manual paste)\n  -h, --help             help for attach\n      --review           Tag the attached session as an agent review\n      --skills strings   Optional: declare which review skills were run in this session. Only used with --review\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n"},"started_at_ms":1791438471025,"completed_at_ms":1791438471025}}
