0,\"original_token_count\":205,\"output\":\"179:index and toolbar to the full Unit label. Header `UNIT_LABEL_SHORT`, navigation\\n180:`LABEL_SHORT` and toolbar `LABEL_SHORT` now compile and render independently.\\n182:Modern `toolbar_unit_label` takes precedence by key presence, followed by\\n183:`toolbar_show_unit_title` and then older `unit_title`; explicit newer empty keys\\n198:add only the new toolbar mode; its other exact assertions and vendor bytes are\\n226:SQLite success is not PostgreSQL or merge acceptance. Toolbar on-primary\\n517:and inactive protection in both interfaces, all three themes, administrator\\n536:Unit-short-label/toolbar-color delta and broader production acceptance remain\\n639:not proof of Original Verona toolbar rendering. The existing six non-saving\\n953:development build (three themes, four viewports, fresh/mixed/long/Review states).\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"e1273b\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000008417,\"exit_code\":1,\"original_token_count\":0,\"output\":\"\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"80dece\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007875,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":156,\"output\":\"ui_smoke_step=action-admin-role-assignments-group_monitor-done\\nui_smoke_step=action-monitor-profile-library-room-overview-start\\nui_smoke_step=action-monitor-profile-library-room-overview-done\\nui_smoke_step=monitor-profile-authoring\\nui_smoke_step=action-admin-role-assignments-tenant_admin-start\\nui_smoke_step=action-admin-role-assignments-tenant_admin-done\\nui_smoke_step=revoke-tenant-admin-role\\nui_smoke_step=action-revoke-role-start\\nui_smoke_step=action-revoke-role-done\\nui_smoke_step=assign-platform-admin-role-with-step-up\\nui_smoke_step=revoke-platform-admin-role-with-step-up\\nui_smoke_step=admin-platform-role-step-up\\n\"}","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_06ef5e23f2db4ce4016ac72be967a08191b78e097f00a31b7b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1199d-3152-75c1-89b7-3e60b92f4af5"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"content":[{"text":"Der vollständige Lauf prüft gerade die Administrationsabläufe; die Teilnehmer- und Player-Abschnitte folgen danach. Daneben zeigt der Quellenvergleich eine konkrete UI-Abweichung: Die optionale Original-Toolbar nutzt noch eine Rewrite-Farbe statt des aktuellen Original-Theme-Tokens.\n","type":"output_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":566},"id":"msg_06ef5e23f2db4ce4016ac72be9815481918e887ca55b41deda","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"create_time":1791437801.5074568,"turn_id":"01a1199d-3152-75c1-89b7-3e60b92f4af5"},"phase":"commentary","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"call_id":"call_d1804c9ebacf408f93258286f780bfa0","id":"ctc_06ef5e23f2db4ce4016ac72beaecfc8191ab6b6d8101f03f73","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat apps/web/src/app/original-player-surface.css apps/web/src/app/original-material-theme.scss\",workdir:\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app\",login:false,max_output_tokens:10000}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rg --files /tmp -g 'playwright-test-*original*' -g 'playwright-test-*label*' -g '*reference*player*'\",\"login\":false,max_output_tokens:2000}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git show --stat 68c883b9\",workdir:\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite\",login:false,max_output_tokens:2000}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '18090,18280p' scripts/smoke-ui.mjs\",workdir:\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app\",login:false,max_output_tokens:7000}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rg '^ui_smoke_step=|^actual_native_whole_error=|^native-controller-event=' /tmp/testcenter-controller-native-whole-20261008.log | tail -12\",login:false,max_output_tokens:1500}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1791437802.9286644,"turn_id":"01a1199d-3152-75c1-89b7-3e60b92f4af5"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_d1804c9ebacf408f93258286f780bfa0","guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000},"id":"ctco_01a11a03-9def-7dc3-a0c3-f02b3d339ba9","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1791437807.087722,"turn_id":"01a1199d-3152-75c1-89b7-3e60b92f4af5"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"623730\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000008583,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":844,\"output\":\"/* Original controller geometry, adapted from IQB Testcenter 19 (MIT). */\\n:root[data-interface-mode=\\\"original\\\"] .page.is-participant-page:has(.is-original-player) {\\n  height: 100dvh;\\n  display: flex;\\n  flex-direction: column;\\n}\\n:root[data-interface-mode=\\\"original\\\"] .page:has(.is-original-player) .participant-topbar { flex: 0 0 auto; }\\n:root[data-interface-mode=\\\"original\\\"] .participant-stage:has(.is-original-player) {\\n  display: flex;\\n  flex: 1;\\n  min-height: 0;\\n}\\n:root[data-interface-mode=\\\"original\\\"] app-participant-view:has(.is-original-player) {\\n  display: flex;\\n  flex: 1;\\n  min-height: 0;\\n}\\n.is-original-player {\\n  display: flex;\\n  flex-direction: column;\\n  flex: 1;\\n  min-height: 0;\\n  gap: 0;\\n}\\n.is-original-player #participantRoutePlayer,\\n.is-original-player #participantRoutePlayer \u003e .record-card {\\n  display: flex;\\n  flex-direction: column;\\n  flex: 1;\\n  min-height: 0;\\n  margin: 0;\\n  padding: 0;\\n  border: 0;\\n  border-radius: 0;\\n  background: white;\\n  box-shadow: none;\\n  gap: 0;\\n}\\n.is-original-player #participantRoutePlayer \u003e h2,\\n.is-original-player .participant-runtime-toolbar,\\n.is-original-player #participantRouteBookletLoadingStatus,\\n.is-original-player .participant-meta-grid,\\n.is-original-player .record-card \u003e header,\\n.is-original-player .record-card \u003e dl,\\n.is-original-player .participant-progress,\\n.is-original-player .participant-draft-state,\\n.is-original-player .participant-completion-readiness,\\n.is-original-player .participant-leave-lock,\\n.is-original-player .record-card \u003e .participant-testlet-timer:not(.is-warning),\\n.is-original-player .record-card \u003e .actions,\\n.is-original-player .verona-player-shell \u003e header,\\n.is-original-player .verona-player-shell \u003e footer:not(:has(button)),\\n.is-original-player .participant-connection-state:not(.is-degraded) { display: none; }\\n.is-original-player app-verona-player-host,\\n.is-original-player .verona-player-shell {\\n  display: flex;\\n  flex-direction: column;\\n  flex: 1;\\n  min-height: 0;\\n  gap: 0;\\n  border: 0;\\n  border-radius: 0;\\n}\\n.is-original-player .verona-player-content {\\n  flex: 1;\\n  min-height: 0;\\n  position: relative;\\n}\\n.is-original-player .verona-player-frame-host { height: 100%; min-height: 0; }\\n.is-original-player .verona-player-frame { height: 100%; min-height: 0; }\\n.is-original-player .participant-review-panel,\\n.is-original-player .unit-rail {\\n  margin: 0;\\n  padding: 15px;\\n  border: 0;\\n  border-radius: 0;\\n  background: white;\\n}\\n.is-original-player .unit-rail-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }\\n.is-original-player .unit-chip { max-width: 100%; }\\n.is-original-player .form-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }\\n.original-player-menu { font-family: 'Nunito Sans', sans-serif; }\\n@use '@angular/material' as mat;\\n@use './original-base-palettes' as palettes;\\n\\n@mixin apply() {\\n  @include mat.theme((\\n    color: (primary: palettes.$primary-palette, tertiary: palettes.$tertiary-palette),\\n    typography: 'Nunito Sans',\\n    density: 0\\n  ));\\n  --mat-sys-primary: var(--secondary);\\n  --mat-sys-secondary: var(--secondary-soft);\\n  --mat-sys-on-primary: #fff;\\n  --mat-sys-primary-container: #fff;\\n  --mat-sys-on-secondary-container: var(--secondary);\\n  --mat-sys-surface: #fff;\\n  --mat-sys-surface-container: #fff;\\n  --mat-sys-outline-variant: var(--secondary);\\n  @include mat.button-overrides((filled-container-shape: 10px, tonal-container-shape: 10px, outlined-container-shape: 10px));\\n}\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"de918c\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007666,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":13,\"output\":\"/tmp/playwright-test-short-unit-labels-20261008.js\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"8a610d\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.00000675,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":383,\"output\":\"commit 68c883b989011a2442454032513baca32c037b3a\\nAuthor: jurei733 \u003c67505990+jurei733@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\\nDate:   Thu Oct 8 01:03:20 2026 +0200\\n\\n    Support independent current Unit labels in both interfaces\\n    \\n    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M4C9QK8NH2R9F0GS8DPSEJBV\\n\\n rewrite-app/README.md                              |   9 +-\\n rewrite-app/apps/api/src/integration.test.ts       |   5 +\\n .../app/original-player-navigation.component.ts    |   2 +-\\n .../src/app/original-player-toolbar.component.ts   |   2 +-\\n .../apps/web/src/app/participant-view.component.ts |   3 +-\\n .../apps/web/src/app/participant-view.facade.ts    |  42 +++--\\n .../web/src/app/verona-player-host.component.ts    |   5 +-\\n rewrite-app/apps/web/src/styles.css                |   7 +\\n rewrite-app/docs/ORIGINAL-UI-PARITY.md             |  20 ++-\\n rewrite-app/docs/PARITY.md                         |  65 +++++++-\\n rewrite-app/package.json                           |   2 +-\\n rewrite-app/packages/application/src/index.ts      |  20 ++-\\n .../packages/contracts/src/booklet-policy.test.ts  |  68 ++++++++\\n .../packages/contracts/src/booklet-policy.ts       |  20 ++-\\n rewrite-app/packages/domain/src/index.ts           |   7 +-\\n .../scripts/participant-unit-label-smoke.mjs       | 150 +++++++++++++++++\\n .../scripts/participant-unit-labels.test.mjs       | 184 +++++++++++++++++++++\\n rewrite-app/scripts/smoke-ui.mjs                   |  11 ++\\n .../current-unit-label-cases.json                  |  12 ++\\n 19 files changed, 595 insertions(+), 39 deletions(-)\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"a7488b\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000006916,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1434,\"output\":\"    .waitFor();\\n  await page.locator(\\\"#participantConfirmationContinueButton\\\").click();\\n  await page.locator(\\\"#participantRouteEntry\\\").waitFor();\\n  const configSeventeenRuntimeState = await (\\n    await sendSmokeJson(\\n      `${baseUrl}/api/v1/participant/sessions/${encodeURIComponent(\\n        configSeventeenBrowser.participantSessionId\\n      )}/runtime-state`,\\n      { method: \\\"GET\\\" }\\n    )\\n  ).json();\\n  assert.equal(\\n    configSeventeenRuntimeState.runtimeState?.runtimeStatus,\\n    \\\"in_progress\\\"\\n  );\\n  assert.equal(\\n    configSeventeenRuntimeState.runtimeState?.availableAction,\\n    \\\"resume\\\"\\n  );\\n\\n  const configEighteenBrowser = await openOriginalBookletConfig(\\n    \\\"Bklt_Config-18\\\",\\n    \\\"Cy-Bklt_BkltConfig-18\\\"\\n  );\\n  await page.locator(\\\"#participantRouteUnitRail\\\").waitFor();\\n  await expectButtonSelectorEnabled(\\\"#participantRouteCompleteButton\\\");\\n  await page.locator(\\\"#participantRouteCompleteButton\\\").click();\\n  await page\\n    .locator(\\\"#participantConfirmationTitle\\\")\\n    .filter({ hasText: \\\"Complete test?\\\" })\\n    .waitFor();\\n  await page.locator(\\\"#participantConfirmationContinueButton\\\").click();\\n  await page.locator(\\\"#participantRouteEntry\\\").waitFor();\\n  assert.equal(\\n    await page.locator(\\\"#participantRouteResumeRunButton\\\").count(),\\n    0\\n  );\\n  const configEighteenLockedState = await (\\n    await sendSmokeJson(\\n      `${baseUrl}/api/v1/participant/sessions/${encodeURIComponent(\\n        configEighteenBrowser.participantSessionId\\n      )}/current-state`,\\n      { method: \\\"GET\\\" }\\n    )\\n  ).json();\\n  assert.equal(\\n    configEighteenLockedState.currentRunState?.testRun?.status,\\n    \\\"paused\\\"\\n  );\\n  assert.equal(\\n    configEighteenLockedState.currentRunState?.testRun?.locked,\\n    true\\n  );\\n  assert.deepEqual(\\n    configEighteenLockedState.currentRunState?.availableActions,\\n    []\\n  );\\n\\n  await openOriginalBookletConfig(\\n    \\\"Bklt_Config-23\\\",\\n    \\\"Cy-Bklt_BkltConfig-23\\\"\\n  );\\n  assert.equal(\\n    await page.locator(\\\"#participantVeronaGlobalForwardButton\\\").count(),\\n    0,\\n    \\\"HIDDEN must omit the separate global forward button.\\\"\\n  );\\n  await openOriginalBookletConfig(\\n    \\\"Bklt_Config-25\\\",\\n    \\\"Cy-Bklt_BkltConfig-25\\\"\\n  );\\n  await expectButtonSelectorEnabled(\\\"#participantVeronaGlobalForwardButton\\\");\\n  await page.locator(\\\"#participantVeronaGlobalForwardButton\\\").click();\\n  await page\\n    .locator(\\\"#participantRouteUnitKey\\\")\\n    .filter({ hasText: \\\"cpy\\\" })\\n    .waitFor({ timeout: 15_000 });\\n  const verifyCurrentPageOnReturn = async (number, expectedPageLabel) =\u003e {\\n    await openOriginalBookletConfig(\\n      `Bklt_Config-${number}`,\\n      `Cy-Bklt_BkltConfig-${number}`\\n    );\\n    await page\\n      .locator(\\\"#participantVeronaPageLabel\\\")\\n      .filter({ hasText: \\\"Page 1/2\\\" })\\n      .waitFor();\\n    await expectButtonSelectorEnabled(\\\"#participantVeronaNextPageButton\\\");\\n    await page.locator(\\\"#participantVeronaNextPageButton\\\").click();\\n    await page\\n      .locator(\\\"#participantVeronaPageLabel\\\")\\n      .filter({ hasText: \\\"Page 2/2\\\" })\\n      .waitFor();\\n    await page.locator(\\\"#participantRouteNextUnitButton\\\").click();\\n    await page\\n      .locator(\\\"#participantRouteUnitKey\\\")\\n      .filter({ hasText: \\\"cpy\\\" })\\n      .waitFor({ timeout: 15_000 });\\n    await page.locator(\\\"#participantRoutePreviousUnitButton\\\").click();\\n    await page\\n      .locator(\\\"#participantRouteUnitKey\\\")\\n      .filter({ hasText: \\\"CY-Unit.Sample-101\\\" })\\n      .waitFor({ timeout: 15_000 });\\n    await page\\n      .locator(\\\"#participantVeronaPageLabel\\\")\\n      .filter({ hasText: expectedPageLabel })\\n      .waitFor({ timeout: 15_000 });\\n  };\\n  await verifyCurrentPageOnReturn(27, \\\"Page 1/2\\\");\\n  await verifyCurrentPageOnReturn(28, \\\"Page 2/2\\\");\\n\\n  await openOriginalBookletConfig(\\n    \\\"Bklt_Config-29\\\",\\n    \\\"Cy-Bklt_BkltConfig-29\\\"\\n  );\\n  await page\\n    .locator(\\\"#participantRouteUnitNavigationLabel\\\")\\n    .filter({ hasText: \\\"Unit 1 / 2\\\" })\\n    .waitFor();\\n\\n  await openOriginalBookletConfig(\\n    \\\"Bklt_Config-30\\\",\\n    \\\"Cy-Bklt_BkltConfig-30\\\"\\n  );\\n  await page\\n    .locator(\\\"#participantRouteUnitNavigationLabel\\\")\\n    .filter({ hasText: \\\"Aufgabe1\\\" })\\n    .waitFor();\\n\\n  await openOriginalBookletConfig(\\n    \\\"Bklt_Config-31\\\",\\n    \\\"Cy-Bklt_BkltConfig-31\\\"\\n  );\\n  assert.equal(\\n    await page.locator(\\\"#participantRouteUnitNavigationLabel\\\").count(),\\n    0\\n  );\\n\\n  await openOriginalBookletConfig(\\n    \\\"Bklt_Config-32\\\",\\n    \\\"Cy-Bklt_BkltConfig-32\\\"\\n  );\\n  await expectButtonSelectorDisabled(\\\"#participantRoutePreviousUnitButton\\\");\\n  await expectButtonSelectorEnabled(\\\"#participantRouteNextUnitButton\\\");\\n\\n  await openOriginalBookletConfig(\\n    \\\"Bklt_Config-33\\\",\\n    \\\"Cy-Bklt_BkltConfig-33\\\"\\n  );\\n  assert.equal(\\n    await page.locator(\\\"#participantRoutePreviousUnitButton\\\").count(),\\n    0\\n  );\\n  assert.equal(\\n    await page.locator(\\\"#participantRouteNextUnitButton\\\").count(),\\n    0\\n  );\\n\\n  await openOriginalBookletConfig(\\n    \\\"Bklt_Config-34\\\",\\n    \\\"Cy-Bklt_BkltConfig-34\\\"\\n  );\\n  await page\\n    .locator(\\\"#participantVeronaPageLabel\\\")\\n    .filter({ hasText: \\\"Page 1/2\\\" })\\n    .waitFor();\\n\\n  await openOriginalBookletConfig(\\n    \\\"Bklt_Config-35\\\",\\n    \\\"Cy-Bklt_BkltConfig-35\\\"\\n  );\\n  await page\\n    .locator(\\\"#participantVeronaPageLabel\\\")\\n    .filter({ hasText: \\\"Aufgabe1: Fieldset1\\\" })\\n    .waitFor();\\n\\n  await openOriginalBookletConfig(\\n    \\\"Bklt_Config-36\\\",\\n    \\\"Cy-Bklt_BkltConfig-36\\\"\\n  );\\n  const pageListItems = page.locator(\\n    \\\"#participantVeronaPageLabel .verona-player-page-list \u003e span\\\"\\n  );\\n  await pageListItems.first().waitFor();\\n  assert.equal(await pageListItems.count(), 2);\\n  assert.equal(await pageListItems.first().getAttribute(\\\"aria-current\\\"), \\\"page\\\");\\n\\n  await openOriginalBookletConfig(\\n    \\\"Bklt_Config-37\\\",\\n    \\\"Cy-Bklt_BkltConfig-37\\\"\\n  );\\n  assert.equal(await page.locator(\\\"#participantVeronaPageLabel\\\").count(), 0);\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"0435fd\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007375,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":137,\"output\":\"ui_smoke_step=admin-required-password-change\\nui_smoke_step=action-sign-out-start\\nui_smoke_step=action-sign-out-done\\nui_smoke_step=action-sign-in-start\\nui_smoke_step=action-sign-in-done\\nui_smoke_step=delegated-workspace-operator-management\\nui_smoke_step=action-create-admin-user-start\\nui_smoke_step=action-create-admin-user-done\\nui_smoke_step=action-admin-users-ui-delegated-admin-1791437802592-start\\nui_smoke_step=action-admin-users-ui-delegated-admin-1791437802592-done\\nui_smoke_step=admin-user-display-name\\nui_smoke_step=admin-user-access-window\\n\"}","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_06ef5e23f2db4ce4016ac72bf86b8c8191af83262ce754e146","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1199d-3152-75c1-89b7-3e60b92f4af5"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_dad0ef175df34c76ab76783d5f1b8745","id":"ctc_06ef5e23f2db4ce4016ac72bf88d948191a66a9137b1916848","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '165,230p' docs/PARITY.md\",workdir:\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app\",login:false,max_output_tokens:6500}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat /tmp/playwright-test-short-unit-labels-20261008.js\",login:false,max_output_tokens:6500}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git log origin/master -6 --oneline\",workdir:\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter\",login:false,max_output_tokens:2000}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rg '^ui_smoke_step=|^actual_native_whole_error=|^native-controller-event=' /tmp/testcenter-controller-native-whole-20261008.log | tail -12\",login:false,max_output_tokens:1500}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1791437816.5556037,"turn_id":"01a1199d-3152-75c1-89b7-3e60b92f4af5"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_dad0ef175df34c76ab76783d5f1b8745","guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000},"id":"ctco_01a11a03-cdcf-7aa2-ba33-3355f4f8c660","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1791437819.343791,"turn_id":"01a1199d-3152-75c1-89b7-3e60b92f4af5"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"7fc35c\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000010375,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1102,\"output\":\"The unchanged `68c883b9` complete protected SQLite/production Chrome sequence\\nfails at the later saved-QR-image Attachment Capture step, before group deletion.\\nAn isolated actual attachment smoke repeats the same missing-target timeout;\\nthe rendered UI reports a scanner timeout and makes no successful target lookup.\\nIt is not a complete-flow pass or evidence that short Unit labels caused the\\nfailure. The precise QR-decoder cause, PostgreSQL snapshot/count failure,\\ncomplete-flow CI, all eight full Original-UI rows and broader production\\nacceptance remain open. This step is not a 100-percent or merge-ready claim.\\n\\n### Current independent short Unit labels (2026-10-08)\\n\\nThe upstream target remains `14c98284590195631750bb2352cb398ca669fe7d`,\\nindependently reverified against remote `master` on 2026-10-08. Actual source\\nconfiguration defaults the header to the Booklet label, navigation to the Unit\\nindex and toolbar to the full Unit label. Header `UNIT_LABEL_SHORT`, navigation\\n`LABEL_SHORT` and toolbar `LABEL_SHORT` now compile and render independently.\\nAbsent or empty `labelshort` falls back to the selected Unit's full label.\\nModern `toolbar_unit_label` takes precedence by key presence, followed by\\n`toolbar_show_unit_title` and then older `unit_title`; explicit newer empty keys\\ndo not fall through to older values. `HIDDEN` remains a rendering decision,\\nnot an authorization or Player-metadata change.\\n\\nOlder immutable snapshots project their previously unsupported short-label\\nsource keys when read. Explicit historical values without those source keys,\\nincluding a hidden header/title, remain unchanged. This does not rewrite a\\nrelease, create/reset a Run, replace a saved answer or alter navigation locks.\\nThe actual facade's Verona `unitTitle` and iframe title remain the full label;\\nthe visual navigation label does not remount or reconfigure the Player.\\n\\nFour compiler and twelve actual-facade/projection/corpus regressions run in\\nthe normal test commands. All 432 core/frontend checks, typecheck and the\\nproduction build pass. All 164 API tests pass separately in memory, file and\\nSQLite (492 total). The official historical corpus's literal policy expectations\\nadd only the new toolbar mode; its other exact assertions and vendor bytes are\\nunchanged. The production initial bundle is 469.98 kB, still under the unchanged\\n470-kB error budget; its existing warning thresholds are not raised.\\n\\nThe new `participant-current-unit-labels` section of the complete repository\\nbrowser smoke uses seven checked-in, source-derived configurations and native\\nBooklet 18.0 XML with aliases of the unchanged pinned Controller Unit/Player.\\nIt performs real UI login in fresh contexts, independent exact labels, a\\nmissing-short-label second Unit, trusted native radio input, forward/backward\\nnavigation, exact durable answer and same-Run hard reload. Its owned strict\\nOriginal-19/immutable-production Chrome 154 run passes all 28 combinations\\n(seven configurations, both interfaces, 1280/390 widths). Operator credential\\nleaks and browser page errors must be zero. Bundled Chromium 147 independently\\npasses the same 28 cases on its own fixture (56 browser cases total). The newly\\nextended whole sequence and fresh publication CI are separate checks.\\n\\nThe initial mobile Rewrite repetition fails because its nested cards shrink\\nthe unchanged Player to 280 pixels while the vendor reserves `9em` on each\\nside. The native radio is clipped behind the form's hit target. Original's\\n390-pixel surface passes the same real input. Only mobile Rewrite Player/card\\npadding is reduced; the final seven mobile Rewrite cases pass without forced\\nclicks, synthetic events, added retry loops, vendor/CSS injection or sandbox changes.\\n\\nThe preceding unchanged `5e69fb1d` complete protected SQLite/production Chrome\\nsequence also passes through monitor, exports and teardown. It is not proof\\nof these new label changes. That publication still has a remote PostgreSQL UI\\nfailure: group deletion reports 45 logs against a previously captured 44-log\\nsnapshot. Its cause and exact deletion evidence remain to be resolved; local\\nSQLite success is not PostgreSQL or merge acceptance. Toolbar on-primary\\ncolors, all eight full-page Original-UI rows and broader production acceptance\\nremain open. This step is not a 100-percent or merge-ready claim.\\n\\n### Original Controller native input after viewport rendering (2026-10-08)\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"794d97\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007667,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":4135,\"output\":\"const TARGET_FRONTEND_ROOT = process.env.TARGET_FRONTEND_ROOT;\\nif (!TARGET_FRONTEND_ROOT) throw new Error('Immutable production frontend required.');\\n(async () =\u003e {\\n  const assert = require('node:assert/strict');\\n  const { spawn } = require('node:child_process');\\n  const fs = require('node:fs/promises');\\n  const { join } = require('node:path');\\n  const { tmpdir } = require('node:os');\\n  const { pathToFileURL } = require('node:url');\\n  const { brotliDecompressSync } = require('node:zlib');\\n  const { chromium } = require('playwright');\\n  const projectRoot = '/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app';\\n  const ts = require(require.resolve('typescript', { paths: [projectRoot] }));\\n  process.chdir(projectRoot);\\n  const root = await fs.mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), 'testcenter-short-labels-browser-'));\\n  console.log('owned_unit_label_artifacts=' + root);\\n  const source = await fs.readFile(join(projectRoot, 'scripts/smoke-ui.mjs'), 'utf8');\\n  const ast = ts.createSourceFile('smoke-ui.mjs', source, ts.ScriptTarget.ES2022, true, ts.ScriptKind.JS);\\n  const zipNames = ['crc32Table', 'crc32', 'createStoredZipBuffer'];\\n  const zipDeclarations = [];\\n  const visit = node =\u003e {\\n    if (ts.isVariableDeclaration(node) \u0026\u0026 zipNames.includes(node.name.getText(ast))) zipDeclarations.push(node.getText(ast));\\n    ts.forEachChild(node, visit);\\n  };\\n  visit(ast);\\n  assert.equal(zipDeclarations.length, zipNames.length);\\n  const { createStoredZipBuffer } = await import('data:text/javascript;base64,' + Buffer.from(\\n    zipDeclarations.map(text =\u003e 'const ' + text + ';').join('\\\\n') + '\\\\nexport { createStoredZipBuffer };').toString('base64'));\\n  const corpusRoot = join(projectRoot, 'test-fixtures/original-testcenter');\\n  const corpus = JSON.parse(await fs.readFile(join(corpusRoot, 'corpus.json'), 'utf8'));\\n  const official = corpus.currentOriginalTestControllerPackage;\\n  const unitFixture = official.units.find(item =\u003e item[1] === 'CY-Unit.Sample-101');\\n  const unit = Buffer.from((await fs.readFile(join(corpusRoot, unitFixture[0]), 'utf8')).trim(), 'base64').toString('utf8');\\n  const player = brotliDecompressSync(Buffer.from(await fs.readFile(join(corpusRoot, official.player.fixture), 'utf8'), 'base64')).toString('utf8');\\n  const { cases } = JSON.parse(await fs.readFile(join(corpusRoot, 'current-unit-label-cases.json'), 'utf8'));\\n  const xmlEscape = value =\u003e value.replaceAll('\u0026', '\u0026amp;').replaceAll('\\\"', '\u0026quot;').replaceAll('\u003c', '\u0026lt;');\\n  const fullA = 'Volle Aufgabe ä/β';\\n  const fullB = 'Zweite volle Aufgabe ä/β';\\n  const shortA = 'Kurz ä/β';\\n  const booklets = cases.map(item =\u003e ({ fileName: 'booklets/' + item.key + '.xml', content:\\n    '\u003c?xml version=\\\"1.0\\\"?\u003e\u003cBooklet xmlns:xsi=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\\\" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation=\\\"https://w3id.org/iqb/spec/testcenter-booklet-xml/18.0\\\"\u003e' +\\n    '\u003cMetadata\u003e\u003cId\u003elabels-' + item.key + '\u003c/Id\u003e\u003cLabel\u003eLabel booklet ' + item.key + '\u003c/Label\u003e\u003c/Metadata\u003e\u003cBookletConfig\u003e' +\\n    Object.entries({ pagingMode: 'buttons', navbar_forward_button: 'UNITS', navbar_backward_button: 'UNITS', unit_responses_buffer_time: '0', ...item.config })\\n      .map(([key, value]) =\u003e '\u003cConfig key=\\\"' + key + '\\\"\u003e' + xmlEscape(value) + '\u003c/Config\u003e').join('') +\\n    '\u003c/BookletConfig\u003e\u003cUnits\u003e\u003cTestlet id=\\\"owned-block\\\" label=\\\"Owned block\\\"\u003e\u003cUnit id=\\\"CY-Unit.Sample-101\\\" alias=\\\"a\\\" label=\\\"' + fullA + '\\\" labelshort=\\\"' + shortA + '\\\"/\u003e' +\\n    '\u003cUnit id=\\\"CY-Unit.Sample-101\\\" alias=\\\"b\\\" label=\\\"' + fullB + '\\\"/\u003e\u003c/Testlet\u003e\u003c/Units\u003e\u003c/Booklet\u003e' }));\\n  const archive = createStoredZipBuffer([...booklets, { fileName: 'units/CY_Unit101.xml', content: unit },\\n    { fileName: 'players/verona-player-simple-6.0.html', content: player }]);\\n  const apiModule = pathToFileURL(join(projectRoot, 'apps/api/dist/apps/api/src/index.js')).href;\\n  const server = spawn(process.execPath, ['--input-type=module', '-e', `\\n    import { createProductionApiServer } from ${JSON.stringify(apiModule)};\\n    const server = await createProductionApiServer();\\n    server.listen(0, '127.0.0.1', () =\u003e process.send({ port: server.address().port }));\\n    process.once('SIGTERM', () =\u003e server.close(() =\u003e process.exit(0)));\\n  `], { cwd: TARGET_FRONTEND_ROOT, stdio: ['ignore', 'ignore', 'inherit', 'ipc'], env: { ...process.env,\\n    FIRST_SLICE_STORE: 'sqlite', FIRST_SLICE_SQLITE_FILE: join(root, 'owned.sqlite'),\\n    FIRST_SLICE_BOOTSTRAP_DEMO: 'true', FIRST_SLICE_OPERATOR_AUTH_REQUIRED: 'true',\\n    FIRST_SLICE_XML_SCHEMA_PROFILE: 'original-19', FIRST_SLICE_XML_SCHEMA_DOWNLOAD: 'false',\\n    FIRST_SLICE_XML_SCHEMA_CACHE: join(projectRoot, '.data/original-xml-schemas') } });\\n  let browser;\\n  let page;\\n  let context;\\n  try {\\n    const port = await new Promise((resolve, reject) =\u003e {\\n      const timer = setTimeout(() =\u003e reject(new Error('Owned API startup timed out')), 20000);\\n      server.once('message', value =\u003e { clearTimeout(timer); resolve(value.port); });\\n      server.once('error', error =\u003e { clearTimeout(timer); reject(error); });\\n      server.once('exit', () =\u003e { clearTimeout(timer); reject(new Error('Owned API exited before ready')); });\\n    });\\n    const baseUrl = 'http://127.0.0.1:' + port;\\n    console.log('owned_unit_label_base_url=' + baseUrl);\\n    let operatorToken;\\n    const api = async (path, body, token = operatorToken) =\u003e {\\n      const response = await fetch(baseUrl + path, { method: body === undefined ? 'GET' : 'POST',\\n        headers: { ...(body === undefined ? {} : { 'content-type': 'application/json' }), ...(token ? { authorization: 'Bearer ' + token } : {}) },\\n        ...(body === undefined ? {} : { body: JSON.stringify(body) }) });\\n      const value = await response.json();\\n      assert.ok(response.ok, path + ': ' + response.status + ' ' + JSON.stringify(value));\\n      return value;\\n    };\\n    operatorToken = (await api('/api/v1/admin/auth/sign-in', { username: 'demo-admin', password: 'REDACTED' })).sessionToken;\\n    if (process.env.LABEL_REPOSITORY_GATE) {\\n      browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: false, channel: process.env.LABEL_BROWSER_CHANNEL || 'chrome' });\\n      console.log('unit_label_browser=' + browser.version());\\n      const { runParticipantUnitLabelSmoke } = await import(pathToFileURL(join(projectRoot, 'scripts/participant-unit-label-smoke.mjs')).href);\\n      await runParticipantUnitLabelSmoke({ browser, baseUrl, tenantKey: 'owned-label-tenant', workspaceKey: 'owned-labels',\\n        unitDocument: unit, playerDocument: player, createZip: createStoredZipBuffer, operatorToken,\\n        sendJson: async (url, { body } = {}) =\u003e {\\n          const response = await fetch(url, { method: 'POST', headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json', authorization: 'Bearer ' + operatorToken }, body: JSON.stringify(body) });\\n          assert.ok(response.ok, url + ': ' + response.status);\\n          return response;\\n        } });\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    await api('/api/v1/tenants/demo-tenant/workspaces', { workspaceKey: 'owned-labels', displayName: 'Owned short Unit label acceptance' });\\n    const workspace = '/api/v1/tenants/demo-tenant/workspaces/owned-labels';\\n    const uploaded = await api(workspace + '/source-packages', { fileName: 'owned-labels.zip', mediaType: 'application/zip', sourceDocument: 'data:application/zip;base64,' + archive.toString('base64') });\\n    const imported = await api(workspace + '/import-jobs', { sourcePackageId: uploaded.sourcePackage.sourcePackageId });\\n    assert.equal(imported.importJob.status, 'completed', JSON.stringify(imported.importJob.diagnostics));\\n    assert.ok(imported.stagedContentRelease?.contentReleaseId);\\n    await api(workspace + '/content-releases/' + imported.stagedContentRelease.contentReleaseId + '/activate', {});\\n    await api(workspace + '/participant-roster', { rosterText: ['rewrite', 'original'].flatMap(ui =\u003e [1280, 390].flatMap(width =\u003e cases.map(item =\u003e ({\\n      loginKey: 'labels-' + item.key + '-' + ui + '-' + width, groupKey: 'owned-labels', bookletKey: 'labels-' + item.key, mode: 'run-hot-return'\\n    })))) });\\n    browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: false, channel: process.env.LABEL_BROWSER_CHANNEL || 'chrome' });\\n    console.log('unit_label_browser=' + browser.version());\\n    const interfaces = process.env.LABEL_INTERFACES?.split(',') || ['rewrite', 'original'];\\n    const widths = process.env.LABEL_WIDTHS?.split(',').map(Number) || [1280, 390];\\n    for (const ui of interfaces) for (const width of widths) for (const item of cases.filter(item =\u003e !process.env.LABEL_CASE || item.key === process.env.LABEL_CASE)) {\\n      const loginKey = 'labels-' + item.key + '-' + ui + '-' + width;\\n      context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width, height: 900 } });\\n      await context.tracing.start({ screenshots: true, snapshots: true, sources: true });\\n      page = await context.newPage();\\n      const errors = [];\\n      page.on('pageerror', error =\u003e errors.push(String(error)));\\n      let operatorLeaks = 0;\\n      page.on('request', request =\u003e {\\n        if (request.url().includes('/api/v1/participant/') \u0026\u0026 request.headers().authorization === 'Bearer ' + operatorToken) operatorLeaks++;\\n      });\\n      await page.goto(baseUrl + '/app/participant?' + new URLSearchParams({ ui, tenantKey: 'demo-tenant', workspaceKey: 'owned-labels' }), { waitUntil: 'networkidle' });\\n      if (ui === 'original') await page.getByLabel('Anmeldename', { exact: true }).fill(loginKey);\\n      else await page.locator('#participantLoginKey').fill(loginKey);\\n      const signingIn = page.waitForResponse(response =\u003e new URL(response.url()).pathname === '/api/v1/participant/auth/sign-in');\\n      const resuming = page.waitForResponse(response =\u003e /\\\\/sessions\\\\/[^/]+\\\\/resume$/.test(new URL(response.url()).pathname));\\n      if (ui === 'original') await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Weiter', exact: true }).click();\\n      else await page.locator('#participantRouteSignInButton').click();\\n      const signedIn = await signingIn;\\n      assert.equal(signedIn.status(), 200);\\n      const identity = await signedIn.json();\\n      assert.notEqual(identity.sessionToken, operatorToken);\\n      // A single assigned saving Booklet starts through the real automatic\\n      // participant-entry workflow. Observe its request before submitting login.\\n      const resumed = await resuming;\\n      assert.equal(resumed.status(), 200);\\n      const runId = (await resumed.json()).testRun.testRunId;\\n      const state = () =\u003e api('/api/v1/participant/sessions/' + identity.participantSession.participantSessionId + '/current-state?testRunId=' + runId, undefined, identity.sessionToken);\\n      await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerVersion').filter({ hasText: 'API 6.0' }).waitFor({ state: ui === 'original' ? 'attached' : 'visible' });\\n      const assertLabels = async (full, short, position) =\u003e {\\n        const waitText = (selector, expected) =\u003e page.waitForFunction(({ selector, expected }) =\u003e\\n          document.querySelector(selector)?.textContent?.trim().replace(/\\\\s+/g, ' ') === expected, { selector, expected });\\n        await page.waitForFunction(expected =\u003e document.querySelector('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame')?.getAttribute('title') === expected, full);\\n        const chosen = mode =\u003e mode === 'short' ? short || full : mode === 'booklet' ? 'Label booklet ' + item.key : full;\\n        const headerSelector = ui === 'original' ? '#participantApplicationHeader h1' : '#participantRouteScreenHeader';\\n        const header = page.locator(headerSelector);\\n        await waitText(headerSelector, chosen(item.header));\\n        assert.equal((await header.textContent()).trim(), chosen(item.header));\\n        const toolbarSelector = ui === 'original' ? '#originalPlayerToolbar [data-cy=\\\"unit-title\\\"]' : '#participantRouteUnit';\\n        const toolbar = page.locator(toolbarSelector);\\n        if (item.toolbar === 'hidden') assert.equal(await toolbar.count(), 0);\\n        else { await waitText(toolbarSelector, chosen(item.toolbar)); assert.equal((await toolbar.textContent()).trim(), chosen(item.toolbar)); }\\n        const navigation = page.locator(ui === 'original' ? '#originalUnitNavigation-label' : '#participantRouteUnitNavigationLabel');\\n        if (item.nav === 'hidden') assert.equal(await navigation.count(), 0);\\n        else {\\n          const expected = item.nav === 'index' ? (ui === 'original' ? 'Aufgabe ' + position + '/2' : 'Unit ' + position + ' / 2') : chosen(item.nav);\\n          await waitText(ui === 'original' ? '#originalUnitNavigation-label' : '#participantRouteUnitNavigationLabel', expected);\\n          assert.equal((await navigation.textContent()).trim().replace(/\\\\s+/g, ' '), expected);\\n        }\\n        assert.equal(await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').getAttribute('title'), full);\\n      };\\n      await assertLabels(fullA, shortA, 1);\\n      const firstState = await state();\\n      assert.equal(firstState.currentRunState.bookletUnits[0].shortLabel, shortA);\\n      assert.equal(firstState.currentRunState.bookletUnits[1].shortLabel, undefined);\\n      await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').scrollIntoViewIfNeeded();\\n      await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').screenshot();\\n      const radio = page.frameLocator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').locator('[data-cy=\\\"TestController-radio1-Aufg1\\\"]');\\n      if (process.env.LABEL_DIAGNOSTICS) {\\n        console.log('unit_label_geometry=' + JSON.stringify({ ui, width, key: item.key,\\n          owner: await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').boundingBox(),\\n          radio: await radio.boundingBox(),\\n          inner: await radio.evaluate(element =\u003e ({ width: innerWidth, height: innerHeight, scrollX, scrollY,\\n            box: element.getBoundingClientRect().toJSON(), checked: element.checked,\\n            hit: document.elementFromPoint(element.getBoundingClientRect().x + element.getBoundingClientRect().width / 2,\\n              element.getBoundingClientRect().y + element.getBoundingClientRect().height / 2)?.outerHTML.slice(0, 300) })) }));\\n      }\\n      await radio.check();\\n      let saved;\\n      for (let attempt = 0; attempt \u003c 100; attempt++) {\\n        const snapshot = await state();\\n        const raw = snapshot.currentRunState.testRun.unitResponses.a;\\n        if (raw \u0026\u0026 JSON.parse(raw).unitState?.dataParts?.answers?.includes('VALUE_CHANGED')) { saved = raw; break; }\\n        await new Promise(resolve =\u003e setTimeout(resolve, 100));\\n      }\\n      assert.ok(saved, 'Native radio answer must be durably saved');\\n      await page.locator(ui === 'original' ? '#participantVeronaGlobalForwardButton' : '#participantRouteNextUnitButton').click();\\n      await assertLabels(fullB, undefined, 2);\\n      await page.locator(ui === 'original' ? '#participantVeronaGlobalBackwardButton' : '#participantRoutePreviousUnitButton').click();\\n      await assertLabels(fullA, shortA, 1);\\n      assert.equal((await state()).currentRunState.testRun.unitResponses.a, saved);\\n      await page.reload({ waitUntil: 'networkidle' });\\n      await page.locator('#participantVeronaPlayerVersion').filter({ hasText: 'API 6.0' }).waitFor({ state: ui === 'original' ? 'attached' : 'visible' });\\n      await assertLabels(fullA, shortA, 1);\\n      assert.equal((await state()).currentRunState.testRun.testRunId, runId);\\n      assert.equal((await state()).currentRunState.testRun.unitResponses.a, saved);\\n      assert.equal(await page.frameLocator('#participantVeronaPlayerFrame').locator('[data-cy=\\\"TestController-radio1-Aufg1\\\"]').isChecked(), true);\\n      assert.equal(operatorLeaks, 0);\\n      assert.deepEqual(errors, []);\\n      await page.screenshot({ path: join(root, ui + '-' + width + '-' + item.key + '.png'), fullPage: true });\\n      await context.tracing.stop({ path: join(root, ui + '-' + width + '-' + item.key + '.zip') });\\n      await context.close();\\n      context = null;\\n      console.log('unit_labels=' + ui + '/' + width + '/' + item.key + ':passed');\\n    }\\n    console.log('unit_labels_all_selected_cases_passed=true');\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    if (page) await page.screenshot({ path: join(root, 'failure.png'), fullPage: true }).catch(() =\u003e {});\\n    if (context) await context.tracing.stop({ path: join(root, 'failure.zip') }).catch(() =\u003e {});\\n    throw error;\\n  } finally {\\n    await browser?.close();\\n    const exited = new Promise(resolve =\u003e server.once('exit', resolve));\\n    server.kill('SIGTERM');\\n    await Promise.race([exited, new Promise(resolve =\u003e setTimeout(resolve, 5000))]);\\n    if (server.exitCode === null) server.kill('SIGKILL');\\n  }\\n})().catch(error =\u003e { console.error('unit_label_browser_error=' + error.message); process.exitCode = 1; });\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"12ac4f\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007333,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":105,\"output\":\"14c982845 [fe] Show unit short label in header, navbar and toolbar\\ndfb7c72f3 [fe] Show toolbar text and icons in on-primary colour\\n6b1adeb05 [be] Test that TestDAO rejects log arrays of the wrong type\\n414fe6b80 [be] Remove unused imports and fix UploadedFile annotation\\n1caf54eb2 [be][infra] Run Mago from a pinned binary in the dev container\\n4b9a1e7f4 Merge pull request #1624 from iqb-berlin/fix/resolve-type-errors\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"8b1ecd\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000008208,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":113,\"output\":\"ui_smoke_step=action-sign-out-start\\nui_smoke_step=action-sign-out-done\\nui_smoke_step=action-sign-in-start\\nui_smoke_step=action-sign-in-done\\nui_smoke_step=action-admin-sessions-start\\nui_smoke_step=action-admin-sessions-done\\nui_smoke_step=admin-session-bulk-revoke\\nui_smoke_step=action-admin-users-start\\nui_smoke_step=action-admin-users-done\\nui_smoke_step=admin-user-bulk-password\\nui_smoke_step=admin-user-bulk-role\\nui_smoke_step=admin-user-bulk-status\\n\"}","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_06ef5e23f2db4ce4016ac72bff438881919247100bb085575f","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1199d-3152-75c1-89b7-3e60b92f4af5"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_f46080a073e0426ca6a9a7daa7169688","id":"ctc_06ef5e23f2db4ce4016ac72bff7c488191871659b6e4c20993","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git show dfb7c72f3 --\",workdir:\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter\",login:false,max_output_tokens:6500}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rg -n 'original.*header|mat-toolbar|toolbar-title|account-button|--mat-sys-on-primary' apps/web/src/app/original-* apps/web/src/app/app.component.* --max-count 14\",workdir:\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app\",login:false,max_output_tokens:6000}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rg '^ui_smoke_step=|^actual_native_whole_error=|^native-controller-event=' /tmp/testcenter-controller-native-whole-20261008.log | tail -10\",login:false,max_output_tokens:1500}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1791437823.4881055,"turn_id":"01a1199d-3152-75c1-89b7-3e60b92f4af5"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_f46080a073e0426ca6a9a7daa7169688","guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000},"id":"ctco_01a11a03-e8b2-72f2-a4bb-6be7bcf3aa3a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1791437826.226881,"turn_id":"01a1199d-3152-75c1-89b7-3e60b92f4af5"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"b7d0a3\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007542,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":459,\"output\":\"commit dfb7c72f34727ec17574f93ad25a58d841e4f288\\nAuthor: rhenck \u003crichard.henck@iqb.hu-berlin.de\u003e\\nDate:   Wed Oct 7 11:27:37 2026 +0200\\n\\n    [fe] Show toolbar text and icons in on-primary colour\\n    \\n    Toolbars got the primary colour as background but kept the default\\n    on-surface text and on-surface-variant icon-button colours, so the\\n    review panel title and its buttons were dark on primary. Set the\\n    matching on-primary colours in the theme and drop the header's\\n    manual h1 colour.\\n    \\n    #1538\\n\\ndiff --git a/frontend/src/app/shared/components/header/header.component.scss b/frontend/src/app/shared/components/header/header.component.scss\\nindex d716af7ca..84aa2be09 100644\\n--- a/frontend/src/app/shared/components/header/header.component.scss\\n+++ b/frontend/src/app/shared/components/header/header.component.scss\\n@@ -25,10 +25,6 @@ mat-toolbar {\\n   height: 100%;\\n }\\n \\n-h1 {\\n-  color: var(--mat-sys-on-primary);\\n-}\\n-\\n .account-button {\\n   background-color: var(--mat-sys-on-primary);\\n   color: var(--mat-sys-primary);\\ndiff --git a/frontend/src/theme/material-overrides.scss b/frontend/src/theme/material-overrides.scss\\nindex 1d9cc6edc..94a7934f5 100644\\n--- a/frontend/src/theme/material-overrides.scss\\n+++ b/frontend/src/theme/material-overrides.scss\\n@@ -2,9 +2,17 @@\\n \\n @mixin overrides {\\n   @include mat.toolbar-overrides((\\n-    container-background-color: var(--mat-sys-primary)\\n+    container-background-color: var(--mat-sys-primary),\\n+    container-text-color: var(--mat-sys-on-primary)\\n   ));\\n \\n+  .mat-toolbar {\\n+    @include mat.icon-button-overrides((\\n+      icon-color: var(--mat-sys-on-primary),\\n+      disabled-icon-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--mat-sys-on-primary) 38%, transparent)\\n+    ));\\n+  }\\n+\\n   @include mat.button-overrides((\\n     filled-container-shape: 10px,\\n     tonal-container-shape: 10px,\\n\"}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"23ba62\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.00000925,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":288,\"output\":\"apps/web/src/app/original-material-theme.scss:12:  --mat-sys-on-primary: #fff;\\napps/web/src/app/original-navigation-control.component.css:3:.nav-button { background: var(--mat-sys-primary); color: var(--mat-sys-on-primary); }\\napps/web/src/app/original-player-surface.css:43:.is-original-player .record-card \u003e header,\\napps/web/src/app/original-player-surface.css:51:.is-original-player .verona-player-shell \u003e header,\\napps/web/src/app/original-participant-account.component.ts:20:      \u003cbutton matIconButton id=\\\"originalParticipantAccountButton\\\" class=\\\"account-button\\\"\\napps/web/src/app/original-participant-account.component.ts:22:        #trigger=\\\"matMenuTrigger\\\" data-cy=\\\"account-button\\\"\u003e\\napps/web/src/app/original-participant-account.component.ts:54:    .account-button { display: block; font-family: revert; font-weight: revert; background: white; color: var(--secondary); border-radius: 12px; }\\napps/web/src/app/original-participant-account.component.ts:55:    .account-button:hover { transform: none; }\\napps/web/src/app/original-player-toolbar.component.ts:17:    \u003cdiv id=\\\"originalPlayerToolbar\\\" class=\\\"toolbar-header\\\" data-cy=\